WEBVTT

00:00.008 --> 00:35.166
Support Admin Watch on
kissasia.cam or kisskh.org

00:08.268 --> 00:10.471
(GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING)

00:39.269 --> 00:40.969
Hi, I'm Mark Kerr
and I'm representing

00:41.071 --> 00:42.434
American freestyle wrestling,

00:42.536 --> 00:45.108
and I'm here
at the World Vale Tudo 3

00:45.210 --> 00:46.737
to prove that it's
the best fighting style.

00:46.839 --> 00:49.508
ANNOUNCER:<i> And that is</i>
<i> wrestler, Mark Kerr.</i>

00:49.610 --> 00:53.216
<i> 6'1'', 260 pounds</i>
<i> from Toledo, Ohio,</i>

00:53.318 --> 00:56.351
<i> and again, his specialty</i>
<i> is freestyle wrestling</i>

00:56.453 --> 00:59.552
<i> and this is</i>
<i> his first professional fight.</i>

00:59.654 --> 01:02.191
<i> This guy, we expect</i>
<i> a lot out of this guy,</i>

01:02.294 --> 01:03.821
<i> 'cause his cornerman,</i>
<i> Richard Hamilton,</i>

01:03.923 --> 01:06.291
<i> who brought in three</i>
<i> of the strongest Americans</i>

01:06.393 --> 01:07.892
<i> to ever step into this ring,</i>

01:07.994 --> 01:10.729
<i> that would be Dan Severn,</i>
<i> Don Frye, and Mark Coleman.</i>

01:10.831 --> 01:13.934
<i> He told us earlier today that</i>
<i> this guy is the best</i>

01:14.036 --> 01:15.304
<i> he has ever seen.</i>

01:15.406 --> 01:16.769
<i> And as he enters the ring</i>
<i> for the first time</i>

01:16.871 --> 01:19.306
<i> in his professional career,</i>
<i> we will see how he holds up</i>

01:19.408 --> 01:21.311
<i> to some of the toughest</i>
<i> competition.</i>

01:22.379 --> 01:24.212
<i> And now coming in</i>
<i> is the biggest here.</i>

01:24.314 --> 01:28.049
<i> Paul Varelans,</i>
<i> 6'8", 330 pounds.</i>

01:28.151 --> 01:29.616
<i> From San Jose, California.</i>

01:29.718 --> 01:32.586
<i> And he's had eight years</i>
<i> of wrestling experience too,</i>

01:32.688 --> 01:35.425
<i> but he's definitely</i>
<i> more skilled on his feet.</i>

01:35.527 --> 01:37.590
<i> And there is Sergio Batarelli</i>
<i> getting the fighters ready</i>

01:37.692 --> 01:39.863
<i> -as we await the opening bell.</i>
-(BELL RINGING)

01:39.965 --> 01:41.667
<i> And this fight is underway!</i>

01:41.769 --> 01:43.235
<i> And Kerr is going at him.</i>

01:43.337 --> 01:45.299
<i> He is trying to take him down.</i>
<i> Can he take him down?</i>

01:45.401 --> 01:47.904
<i> Oh! A massive takedown</i>
<i> on Varelans.</i>

01:48.007 --> 01:50.040
<i> A double leg takedown by Kerr.</i>

01:50.142 --> 01:51.636
<i> Look at him jockey</i>
<i> for position.</i>

01:51.738 --> 01:53.172
<i> Wrestling skills</i>
<i> on full display and...</i>

01:53.274 --> 01:54.913
<i> Oh! A knee to the face!</i>

01:55.015 --> 01:56.407
<i> Wow! A magnificent knee</i>
<i> to the face</i>

01:56.510 --> 01:58.150
<i> and another knee to the face.</i>

01:58.252 --> 01:59.951
<i> I'll tell you what.</i>
<i> Varelans is one tough kid,</i>

02:00.053 --> 02:01.718
<i> but he's taking</i>
<i> some brutal shots</i>

02:01.820 --> 02:02.713
<i> to the face here.</i>

02:02.816 --> 02:04.415
<i> His face is getting</i>
<i> destroyed right now.</i>

02:04.517 --> 02:06.321
<i> Batarelli is watching on.</i>

02:06.424 --> 02:08.024
<i> He has...</i>
<i> Yes, he has stopped the fight.</i>

02:08.126 --> 02:09.191
<i> -It is over.</i>
-(BELL RINGING)

02:09.293 --> 02:10.823
ANNOUNCER:
<i> And Kerr wins his debut.</i>

02:10.925 --> 02:13.831
<i> That's right. Varelans was</i>
<i> unable to stop the fight.</i>

02:13.933 --> 02:15.232
<i> Batarelli had to step in.</i>

02:15.334 --> 02:18.229
<i> Whoa. Look at that.</i>
<i> Some serious cuts there.</i>

02:18.331 --> 02:19.300
(IMPERCEPTIBLE)

02:19.402 --> 02:20.598
-Is he fine?
-(SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY)

02:20.700 --> 02:23.635
Okay. Take your time.
Take your time.

02:23.737 --> 02:26.170
Come on. I got you.
Come on. I got you.

02:26.272 --> 02:27.646
Come sit down.

02:27.748 --> 02:29.648
SERGIO: TKO. Ref stop.

02:29.750 --> 02:30.743
CORNERMAN: There you go.

02:31.779 --> 02:33.951
Do you know who you are?
Do you know who you are?

02:34.053 --> 02:35.286
(BREATHING HEAVILY)
In a fight.

02:35.388 --> 02:37.087
CORNERMAN: Yes, you was
in a fight. How did it go?

02:37.189 --> 02:39.353
-You know what happened?
-PAUL: I... lost.

02:39.455 --> 02:40.757
Can I ask him
if he's going to be okay?

02:40.859 --> 02:41.894
I just wanna know.

02:41.996 --> 02:43.320
He'll be fine, Mark.
He'll be fine.

02:43.422 --> 02:44.823
Back to your corner.

02:46.897 --> 02:48.827
(CROWD CHEERING)

02:54.737 --> 02:57.473
-SERGIO: Folks, we ready?
-Just five seconds, please.

02:59.041 --> 03:01.246
(CROWD CHEERING)

03:02.380 --> 03:03.607
INTERVIEWER 1:<i> And what are</i>
<i> you thinking</i>

03:03.709 --> 03:04.975
<i> at the beginning</i>
<i> of the fight?</i>

03:05.077 --> 03:07.117
MARK:<i> You know, the...</i>
<i> the second that bell rings,</i>

03:07.219 --> 03:08.214
<i> you can just look</i>
<i> at some people</i>

03:08.316 --> 03:09.680
<i> and you can just tell</i>

03:09.782 --> 03:12.155
<i> that... that they're</i>
<i> scared to death.</i>

03:12.257 --> 03:13.685
<i> I mean, you can see</i>
<i> in their eyes.</i>

03:13.787 --> 03:15.687
<i> You can even smell it</i>
<i> in their sweat.</i>

03:15.789 --> 03:17.429
INTERVIEWER 1:<i> Wow.</i>
MARK:<i> But you know,</i>

03:17.531 --> 03:19.692
<i> it isn't until the first time</i>
<i> I can put my hands on them,</i>

03:19.794 --> 03:22.696
<i> and really assert myself</i>
<i> on the other person</i>

03:22.798 --> 03:25.763
<i> that you can really feel,</i>
<i> like almost instantly,</i>

03:25.866 --> 03:28.303
<i> if the person is going to</i>
<i> give in or not.</i>

03:28.405 --> 03:29.366
INTERVIEWER 1:
<i> So, what happens next?</i>

03:29.468 --> 03:31.473
MARK:<i> It's simple.</i>

03:31.575 --> 03:34.373
<i> Am I going to hurt him</i>
<i> before he hurts me?</i>

03:34.476 --> 03:35.707
<i> And if he happens to hurt me,</i>

03:35.810 --> 03:38.013
<i> then I am gonna hurt him</i>
<i> two times as bad.</i>

03:38.115 --> 03:39.216
(INTERVIEWER 1 CHUCKLES)

03:39.319 --> 03:40.447
MARK:<i> 'Cause,</i>
<i> let me tell you something,</i>

03:40.549 --> 03:41.853
<i> when you get punched</i>
<i> in the face,</i>

03:41.955 --> 03:43.382
<i> you can have two reactions.</i>

03:43.484 --> 03:45.390
<i> You can either cower away,</i>

03:45.492 --> 03:49.025
<i> or you can want to punish</i>
<i> the person for punching you.</i>

03:49.127 --> 03:51.230
<i> But I developed a third way.</i>

03:51.332 --> 03:54.197
<i> You know, if I get kicked</i>
<i> or if I get punched,</i>

03:54.299 --> 03:55.562
<i> I'm going to</i>
<i> something different</i>

03:55.665 --> 03:57.434
<i> -than punish you.</i>
-(INTERVIEWER 1 CHUCKLES)

03:57.536 --> 04:01.239
<i> I'm going to physically</i>
<i> impose my will on to you.</i>

04:01.341 --> 04:04.304
<i> And you... you really feel</i>
<i> when that happens,</i>

04:04.407 --> 04:06.277
<i> when the person just lets go,</i>

04:06.379 --> 04:08.746
<i> and he totally withers away</i>
<i> in your arms.</i>

04:08.848 --> 04:10.509
<i> And that's...</i>

04:10.611 --> 04:12.810
<i> That's a pretty</i>
<i> powerful thing.</i>

04:12.912 --> 04:15.579
<i> It is crazy</i>
<i> because in the beginning,</i>

04:15.682 --> 04:17.519
<i> I was just kind of having fun.</i>

04:17.621 --> 04:20.186
<i> I was operating</i>
<i> on this animal instinct that</i>

04:20.288 --> 04:21.590
<i> just took over.</i>

04:23.295 --> 04:24.796
<i> Uh, I'm gonna try</i>
<i> and explain it,</i>

04:24.898 --> 04:25.790
<i> and maybe in this way,</i>

04:25.893 --> 04:28.331
<i> but it's... it's kind of</i>
<i> strange, you know?</i>

04:28.433 --> 04:31.831
<i> The whole thing felt</i>
<i> very evolutionary.</i>

04:32.666 --> 04:33.833
<i> I mean, I wrestled in college,</i>

04:33.935 --> 04:37.273
<i> but... but this is</i>
<i> something totally different.</i>

04:37.375 --> 04:38.707
INTERVIEWER 1:
<i> Well, what do you mean?</i>

04:38.809 --> 04:42.510
MARK:<i> Like the moment I felt</i>
<i> that rush, that first hit,</i>

04:42.612 --> 04:44.783
<i> I realized I was getting</i>
<i> pretty close to</i>

04:44.885 --> 04:46.213
<i> something that's...</i>

04:46.315 --> 04:48.148
<i> It's almost magical.</i>

04:48.250 --> 04:49.415
INTERVIEWER 1:<i> Wow.</i>

04:49.517 --> 04:50.484
MARK:<i> You get to the point</i>

04:50.586 --> 04:52.222
<i> where you have to</i>
<i> ask yourself,</i>

04:52.324 --> 04:53.484
<i> like, would you stick</i>
<i> your finger</i>

04:53.586 --> 04:54.686
<i> in your opponent's cut?</i>

04:54.788 --> 04:56.355
<i> Spread it out</i>
<i> a little bit more?</i>

04:56.457 --> 04:57.623
<i> Just... Just to win?</i>

04:57.725 --> 04:59.428
<i> To make him feel pain?</i>
<i> Would you?</i>

04:59.530 --> 05:01.132
INTERVIEWER 1:<i> I mean,</i>
<i> I guess I would.</i>

05:01.234 --> 05:02.763
MARK: (CHUCKLING)
<i> Of course you would.</i>

05:03.265 --> 05:04.467
<i> You know why?</i>

05:04.569 --> 05:07.437
<i> Because winning is</i>
<i> the best feeling there is.</i>

05:07.539 --> 05:08.833
INTERVIEWER 1:<i> Yeah.</i>
MARK:<i> And keep in mind,</i>

05:08.935 --> 05:10.768
<i> this was a tournament</i>
<i> down in Brazil.</i>

05:10.870 --> 05:12.673
<i> So if you won,</i>
<i> you didn't go home.</i>

05:12.775 --> 05:15.609
<i> No. You went on</i>
<i> and you fought the next guy,</i>

05:15.712 --> 05:17.007
<i> and then the next guy</i>
<i> right after that,</i>

05:17.109 --> 05:19.546
<i> and then the next guy,</i>
<i> and then the next guy.</i>

05:19.648 --> 05:23.251
<i> So, by the end,</i>
<i> you felt like a god.</i>

05:23.354 --> 05:25.189
INTERVIEWER 1:<i> Sounds amazing.</i>

05:25.291 --> 05:27.018
<i> -It's incredible.</i>
-(MARK CHUCKLES)

05:32.427 --> 05:33.428
<i> Honestly, when you win,</i>

05:33.530 --> 05:35.664
<i> nothing else</i>
<i> in this world matters.</i>

05:37.436 --> 05:38.600
<i> And it kind of might be</i>
<i> the best feeling</i>

05:38.702 --> 05:40.568
<i> -in the world, you know?</i>
-INTERVIEWER 1:<i> Yeah.</i>

05:40.671 --> 05:42.268
MARK:<i> And it's a feeling</i>
<i> I didn't even know</i>

05:42.370 --> 05:43.606
<i> was possible.</i>

05:43.708 --> 05:45.704
<i> I mean, fuck, man,</i>
<i> I'm getting chills right now</i>

05:45.806 --> 05:47.874
<i> just... just telling you</i>
<i> about this.</i>

06:07.728 --> 06:10.899
Uh, so, Moti...
Uh, The Hammer.

06:11.001 --> 06:11.729
Yeah.

06:11.831 --> 06:14.205
He has experience
in the Octagon.

06:14.307 --> 06:17.838
Uh, you don't.
He's tough. Super tough.

06:18.473 --> 06:19.539
What is it that you think

06:19.641 --> 06:20.739
you're gonna bring
to this fight?

06:20.841 --> 06:22.343
Well, I think that
I feel really good

06:22.445 --> 06:24.075
about my cardiovascular level.

06:24.177 --> 06:27.278
I feel great about my power,
which I've improved on.

06:27.380 --> 06:28.781
(INHALES)

06:28.883 --> 06:30.254
But you know what,
it's like the difference

06:30.356 --> 06:32.853
between a flashlight
and a laser beam.

06:34.056 --> 06:35.524
Wow.

06:35.626 --> 06:37.758
That's awesome.
What do you mean by that?

06:37.860 --> 06:40.426
I have to make sure that
I'm a 100% concentrated

06:40.528 --> 06:42.100
on what I have to do.

06:42.202 --> 06:43.663
Because if not,
then my emotions

06:43.765 --> 06:45.036
will be running
around everywhere,

06:45.138 --> 06:46.301
like a flashlight. (CHUCKLING)

06:46.404 --> 06:47.337
Yeah, that makes
sense, actually.

06:47.439 --> 06:48.404
MARK: Yeah. I mean,
think about it.

06:48.506 --> 06:49.735
It applies to you
and everybody else

06:49.837 --> 06:50.901
-in this room.
-INTERVIEWER 1: Sure.

06:51.003 --> 06:52.576
If we don't control
our emotions,

06:52.678 --> 06:55.177
our fears and our anxieties
will get the best of us.

06:55.279 --> 06:56.811
And you know what happens?

06:56.913 --> 06:58.715
We get slapped around
by our emotions... (CHUCKLES)

06:58.817 --> 07:00.447
-...and we can't have that.
-INTERVIEWER 1: That's right.

07:00.550 --> 07:02.452
-Right?
-COLEMAN: Hey, Kerr.

07:02.554 --> 07:03.914
Get your ass up.
They're all waiting, buddy.

07:04.016 --> 07:05.323
INTERVIEWER 1:
Hey, thank you so much

07:05.426 --> 07:06.356
-for your time.
-Yeah. Thank you very much.

07:06.458 --> 07:08.323
-I appreciate it.
-I appreciate you.

07:08.426 --> 07:09.722
-Ready? Good to see you.
-My man.

07:09.824 --> 07:10.822
-Hey, the only difference...
-Yeah.

07:10.924 --> 07:12.360
...is the shape of the ring,
all right?

07:12.463 --> 07:13.898
-A cage.
-(CHUCKLES) It's a cage.

07:14.000 --> 07:15.362
I know. I know.

07:15.464 --> 07:16.698
First time in the Octagon.

07:16.800 --> 07:17.761
INTERVIEWER 1: I was
telling him the same thing.

07:17.864 --> 07:18.996
-Right.
-Yo, guys, come on.

07:19.099 --> 07:21.306
There's only been
14 of these fucking things.

07:21.408 --> 07:22.470
-He's a killer.
-INTERVIEWER 2: Excuse me.

07:22.572 --> 07:23.637
-Coleman?
-COLEMAN: Yeah, yeah.

07:23.739 --> 07:25.068
INTERVIEWER 2:
Vidmark Entertainment.

07:25.171 --> 07:26.772
Can I ask about your plans
to take on Bobish?

07:26.874 --> 07:30.480
-Oh, Bobish. Um... Kerr?
-MARK: Yeah?

07:30.582 --> 07:31.811
-COLEMAN: Get him down early.
-You got it.

07:31.913 --> 07:33.683
-I'm gonna go warm up.
-COLEMAN: All right.

07:35.417 --> 07:37.189
Sorry. Where was I?

07:37.291 --> 07:38.721
Uh, you were
talking about Bobish.

07:41.589 --> 07:43.792
(INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING)

07:47.134 --> 07:49.127
(CROWD CHEERING IN DISTANCE)

07:56.609 --> 07:59.110
COMMENTATOR 1:<i> And now</i>
<i> we get to the big boys.</i>

07:59.212 --> 08:01.276
<i> Mark Kerr making his debut</i>

08:01.378 --> 08:03.876
<i> against Moti Horenstein,</i>

08:03.978 --> 08:05.747
<i> who is making his</i>
<i> second appearance</i>

08:05.849 --> 08:09.453
<i> in the Octagon losing</i>
<i> only to Mark Coleman.</i>

08:09.555 --> 08:14.325
<i> And here comes</i>
<i> 255-pound, Mark Kerr,</i>

08:14.427 --> 08:17.391
<i> a former Division 1</i>
<i> NCAA champion</i>

08:17.493 --> 08:19.022
<i> at Syracuse University.</i>

08:19.124 --> 08:20.362
ANNOUNCER 1:
<i> Ladies and gentlemen,</i>

08:20.464 --> 08:22.158
<i> it's time for the big men,</i>

08:22.261 --> 08:25.537
<i> as we begin</i>
<i> our heavyweight tournaments.</i>

08:26.572 --> 08:29.473
<i> Standing to my left,</i>
<i> he's the winner of</i>

08:29.576 --> 08:34.143
<i> the 1994 World Cup</i>
<i> Wrestling Championship,</i>

08:34.245 --> 08:35.172
<i> the winner of</i>

08:35.274 --> 08:37.808
<i> the Men's Freestyle National</i>
<i> Championship,</i>

08:37.910 --> 08:40.919
<i> an NCAA Division 1 champion,</i>

08:41.021 --> 08:42.685
<i> he stands 6'1",</i>

08:42.787 --> 08:46.316
<i> -and weighs in at 255 pounds.</i>
-(CROWD CHEERING)

08:46.418 --> 08:48.855
ANNOUNCER 1:<i> He's fighting out</i>
<i> of Phoenix, Arizona,</i>

08:48.957 --> 08:52.157
<i> please welcome</i>
<i> in his Octagon debut,</i>

08:52.592 --> 08:55.765
<i> Mark Kerr!</i>

09:08.243 --> 09:09.240
Hi.

09:12.516 --> 09:13.948
Probably looking at my eyes.

09:15.983 --> 09:17.215
-How did that happen?
-(CHUCKLING)

09:18.423 --> 09:19.489
Well, have you ever heard of

09:19.591 --> 09:21.287
the Ultimate
Fighting Championship?

09:21.389 --> 09:22.792
The UFC?

09:22.894 --> 09:24.996
They were kind of like
the first in combat sports.

09:25.098 --> 09:26.431
Is that boxing?

09:26.533 --> 09:28.496
Well, there's
a little boxing in it. Yeah.

09:28.598 --> 09:30.600
It's more like martial arts

09:30.703 --> 09:32.429
that have been around
for thousands of years

09:32.531 --> 09:37.067
and we bring them all together
to see which one is the best.

09:37.169 --> 09:40.375
So, I come
from a wrestling background,

09:40.477 --> 09:41.609
but I might fight a guy

09:41.711 --> 09:43.074
who comes
from a karate background

09:43.176 --> 09:44.811
or a guy who comes
from a boxing background

09:44.913 --> 09:46.848
-as well.
-Yeah, I've heard about this.

09:46.950 --> 09:49.016
That's the bloody thing
they're trying to ban.

09:49.118 --> 09:52.019
(CHUCKLING) Yes, that's right.
That's right, it is.

09:52.121 --> 09:55.626
But I gotta tell you,
the popularity of the sport

09:55.728 --> 09:58.088
comes from the stereotype
that you're gonna see

09:58.190 --> 10:00.960
the bloodiest
and the goriest sport

10:01.062 --> 10:02.759
-you've ever seen.
-Yeah, I can't do that.

10:02.861 --> 10:04.468
It... it bothers me.

10:04.570 --> 10:06.833
And it should bother
a lot of people.

10:06.935 --> 10:08.772
Do you hate each other
when you fight?

10:09.439 --> 10:10.441
Absolutely not.

10:10.543 --> 10:12.507
PEGGY: Oh.
MARK: Absolutely not. No.

10:12.609 --> 10:13.904
NURSE: Uh, sorry to interrupt.

10:14.007 --> 10:15.740
Uh, Dr. Cortez
can see you now.

10:15.842 --> 10:17.176
Great. Thank you so much.

10:18.483 --> 10:19.749
It was great to talk to you.

10:19.851 --> 10:21.679
Thank you. It was great
to talk with you, too.

10:21.781 --> 10:23.349
(MARK CLEARS THROAT)

10:23.451 --> 10:24.623
Here.

10:26.490 --> 10:27.659
What's up, little man?

10:27.761 --> 10:29.152
-I'm sorry. He's kind of shy.
-MARK: That's okay.

10:29.254 --> 10:30.524
But I think he wants
your autograph.

10:30.626 --> 10:31.624
MARK: Sure, no problem.

10:31.726 --> 10:33.429
Wh... What's your name?

10:33.531 --> 10:35.766
(CHUCKLES) His name is Cosmo.

10:35.868 --> 10:38.232
But could you make it out
to his brother, Murray, too?

10:38.334 --> 10:39.396
Sure.

10:40.437 --> 10:41.706
(SOFTLY) Cosmo.

10:45.177 --> 10:46.205
No fighting.

11:06.760 --> 11:08.499
(KNOCK ON DOOR)

