STEPHEN QUADROS:
<i> We've got Kerr,</i>

28:05.543 --> 28:09.882
<i> the quintessential wrestler,</i>
<i> the takedown artist,</i>

28:09.984 --> 28:12.054
<i> against maybe</i>
<i> the purest puncher</i>

28:12.590 --> 28:13.785
<i> in the game, Igor Vovchanchyn.</i>

28:13.887 --> 28:15.558
<i> And there's Mark Coleman,</i>

28:15.660 --> 28:18.960
<i> a former three-time</i>
<i> UFC champion,</i>

28:19.859 --> 28:22.326
<i> uh, cornering Mark Kerr.</i>

28:23.997 --> 28:26.403
<i> So, you know, he's gonna be...</i>

28:26.505 --> 28:28.101
I'm gonna go
find my seat, okay.

28:35.974 --> 28:39.715
ANNOUNCER:<i> Mark Kerr!</i>

28:39.817 --> 28:41.317
BAS:<i> On paper,</i>
<i> I would say Mark Kerr's</i>

28:41.419 --> 28:42.178
<i> going to win the fight.</i>

28:42.280 --> 28:43.617
STEPHEN QUADROS:
<i> I would say it too,</i>

28:43.720 --> 28:46.656
<i> but Vovchanchyn may have faced</i>

28:46.759 --> 28:50.486
<i> a tougher caliber opponent</i>
<i> than Kerr has.</i>

28:50.588 --> 28:54.095
BAS:<i> Yeah, that's what</i>
<i> most people say, but if...</i>

28:54.664 --> 28:55.929
<i> But I'll tell you one thing.</i>

28:56.032 --> 29:00.599
<i> Vovchanchyn has never faced</i>
<i> a Mark Kerr,</i>

29:00.701 --> 29:01.767
<i> but let's be fair.</i>

29:01.870 --> 29:03.002
<i> On the other side of the coin,</i>

29:03.105 --> 29:06.070
<i> Kerr has never faced</i>
<i> a striker, possibly,</i>

29:06.172 --> 29:08.944
<i> as dangerous as</i>
<i> Igor Vovchanchyn.</i>

29:09.046 --> 29:12.449
STEPHEN QUADROS:<i> This is</i>
<i> a monumental battle here.</i>

29:12.551 --> 29:15.016
-(DRUMS BEATING)
-(CROWD CHEERING)

29:30.897 --> 29:32.066
COLEMAN: Let's go, Kerr.

29:38.170 --> 29:39.708
(REFEREE SPEAKING
INDISTINCTLY)

29:39.810 --> 29:41.610
(COLEMAN SPEAKING
INDISTINCT INSTRUCTIONS)

29:41.712 --> 29:43.708
-(BELL RINGS)
-(CROWD CHEERING)

29:43.810 --> 29:45.112
COLEMAN: Move! Move!

29:46.647 --> 29:48.277
Legs! Legs!

29:48.379 --> 29:50.414
(IGOR'S CORNERMAN
SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY)

29:52.456 --> 29:53.483
COLEMAN: Pressure.

29:54.921 --> 29:56.118
Lock his hands, Kerr.

29:56.220 --> 29:58.260
Come on, Mark! Let's go, baby!

29:58.362 --> 29:59.390
Play smart!

30:00.199 --> 30:01.227
There we go.

30:01.728 --> 30:03.361
(ALL EXCLAIM)

30:04.095 --> 30:05.429
COLEMAN: Under takedown!

30:06.397 --> 30:08.234
-Get it!
-(MAN YELLING INDISTINCTLY)

30:10.208 --> 30:11.338
Let's go!

30:11.940 --> 30:13.877
Use your hands.
Use your hands.

30:14.578 --> 30:16.810
There we go! Pull! Pull!

30:16.912 --> 30:18.547
-Keep him down.
-Come on, Mark!

30:18.649 --> 30:20.283
(MAN SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY)

30:20.385 --> 30:22.686
COLEMAN: Come on.

30:22.788 --> 30:24.954
(UKRAINIAN CORNERMAN
SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY)

30:26.051 --> 30:27.352
COLEMAN: There we go.

30:31.630 --> 30:33.858
-Get up!
-Get up, Mark! Get up!

30:33.960 --> 30:36.460
COLEMAN: Get up! Hands up!

30:37.764 --> 30:38.798
(CROWD CHEERING)

30:38.900 --> 30:40.563
Go! Keep going! Keep going!

30:41.273 --> 30:42.532
Nice! Nice!

30:44.002 --> 30:45.172
Get him! Get him!

30:46.742 --> 30:48.241
He's got your head, Mark.

30:49.240 --> 30:50.980
(MAN SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY)

30:52.345 --> 30:54.648
Detach yourself, buddy!
Get up right now!

30:54.750 --> 30:56.953
(JARRING MUSIC PLAYING)

30:58.524 --> 30:59.923
You gotta get up right now!

31:01.020 --> 31:02.618
Get up, Mark! Come on!

31:04.794 --> 31:06.093
Move, buddy! You got to move!

31:06.195 --> 31:08.726
Protect yourself, buddy!
Get up! Move right now!

31:08.828 --> 31:10.329
Kerr, move!

31:10.763 --> 31:12.194
Come on.

31:12.297 --> 31:13.834
-Get up, Kerr!
-(MARK GROANS)

31:13.936 --> 31:15.631
You gotta go!
You gotta get up!

31:16.675 --> 31:18.938
(REFEREE
SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY)

31:19.040 --> 31:20.911
STEPHEN QUADROS:
<i> And Kerr is out!</i>

31:21.578 --> 31:23.010
BAS:<i> Oh, my God!</i>

31:23.112 --> 31:24.348
STEPHEN QUADROS:
<i> Kerr has been knocked out</i>

31:24.450 --> 31:25.779
<i> by Igor Vovchanchyn!</i>

31:25.882 --> 31:29.246
<i> On his knees, but... but wait.</i>

31:29.348 --> 31:32.186
<i> Vovchanchyn is wild</i>
<i> in celebration.</i>

31:33.019 --> 31:35.123
<i> He slayed the beast.</i>

31:36.155 --> 31:37.554
MARK: How is that not illegal?

31:38.761 --> 31:40.357
How is that not illegal?

31:40.459 --> 31:42.392
How is that not illegal on top
of my head?

31:42.494 --> 31:44.201
-It's illegal.
-(APOLOGIZING IN JAPANESE)

31:44.303 --> 31:45.330
No, no, no.

31:45.432 --> 31:46.569
STEPHEN QUADROS:<i> Oh,</i>
<i> you know what it was?</i>

31:46.671 --> 31:47.562
BAS:<i> I think it was a foul.</i>

31:47.665 --> 31:48.965
<i> There are no knees</i>
<i> allowed on the ground.</i>

31:49.067 --> 31:50.001
<i> He's no force.</i>

31:50.104 --> 31:51.370
STEPHEN QUADROS:<i> That's right.</i>

31:51.472 --> 31:54.544
<i> That's right. There are</i>
<i> no knees allowed to the head</i>

31:54.647 --> 31:56.842
<i> when an opponent is all but...</i>

31:56.944 --> 31:59.147
(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

32:05.654 --> 32:06.616
It's okay, baby.

32:13.095 --> 32:14.731
STEPHEN QUADROS:
<i> The referee has raised</i>

32:14.833 --> 32:18.232
<i> Igor Vovchanchyn's arm</i>
<i> in victory.</i>

32:19.802 --> 32:21.972
(TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES)

32:37.348 --> 32:40.617
(SAKAKIBARA SPEAKING JAPANESE)

32:43.193 --> 32:45.795
-(IN ENGLISH) Mr. Sakakibara?
-SAKAKIBARA: Yes?

32:45.897 --> 32:47.155
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.
How are you?

32:47.257 --> 32:48.829
I am fine. And you?

32:48.931 --> 32:50.663
I'm not good. I'm not good.

32:50.765 --> 32:52.330
Bad referee.

32:52.432 --> 32:55.698
Bad... Vovchanchyn bam
on top of the head.

32:56.739 --> 32:58.640
It's wrong. Foul.

32:58.742 --> 32:59.940
Referee no call foul.

33:00.042 --> 33:01.137
And then twice,
two more times,

33:01.239 --> 33:03.813
bam on top of my head.

33:03.915 --> 33:05.011
And I was laying
on the ground waiting

33:05.113 --> 33:06.814
for the referee
to call a foul.

33:06.916 --> 33:08.577
He didn't call foul. (PANTING)

33:08.680 --> 33:11.183
It's wrong. It's illegal
on top of the head. Bam.

33:11.285 --> 33:12.854
-Okay. Okay. I talk to him.
-Twice.

33:12.956 --> 33:14.752
-Please. Please.
-Okay? Yeah, okay.

33:14.854 --> 33:16.086
<i> Arigato.</i>

33:16.188 --> 33:17.489
-I didn't lose.
-Yeah.

33:22.800 --> 33:25.464
(SAKAKIBARA SPEAKING JAPANESE)

33:29.133 --> 33:30.403
(ELEVATOR DINGS)

33:38.142 --> 33:40.347
(ELEVATOR DINGS)

33:56.634 --> 33:57.595
(MARK SNIFFLES)

33:58.603 --> 33:59.597
(ELEVATOR DINGING)

34:14.986 --> 34:16.614
(INDISTINCT ELEVATOR
ANNOUNCEMENT)

34:54.657 --> 34:56.654
(SOBBING)

35:06.935 --> 35:09.106
(CONTINUES SOBBING)

35:19.778 --> 35:21.244
COLEMAN:<i> You've got</i>
<i> some bumps and bruises.</i>

35:21.346 --> 35:22.985
<i> You're not injured.</i>

35:23.087 --> 35:26.081
You'll heal up
in a week or two, tops.

35:26.183 --> 35:27.521
Okay?

35:28.057 --> 35:30.659
(CLEARS THROAT) Yeah. Yeah.

35:30.761 --> 35:32.456
Yeah, that's right.

35:32.558 --> 35:34.824
I'll heal up in a week
or two, tops.

35:36.200 --> 35:38.001
(SNIFFLES) I mean,
my hands aren't broken.

35:38.103 --> 35:40.234
-My... my feet are fine.
-COLEMAN: Mmm-hmm.

35:40.336 --> 35:43.335
(INHALES) My head's
a little banged up.

35:43.437 --> 35:45.241
Igor is one tough
motherfucker, huh?

35:45.343 --> 35:46.773
MARK: Tough motherfucker.
COLEMAN: I'll give him that.

35:46.875 --> 35:48.708
(MARK CHUCKLING)

35:48.810 --> 35:49.806
Yeah.

35:50.241 --> 35:51.511
Thank you.

35:54.351 --> 35:55.644
COLEMAN: All right, guys,
I'm gonna run outside.

35:55.746 --> 35:58.716
-I'll be back, okay?
-MARK: Yeah, yeah.

36:02.787 --> 36:05.423
Hey, Coleman,
um, can I just talk to you?

36:05.525 --> 36:07.258
-Yeah.
-Sorry. I just want to know

36:07.361 --> 36:08.691
if he... if he's
gonna be okay.

36:08.794 --> 36:11.328
I've never seen him
like this before, so...

36:11.430 --> 36:12.801
-He should be fine.
-Okay.

36:12.903 --> 36:14.033
And he seemed okay, right?

36:14.135 --> 36:15.733
Yeah, I mean, I just...

36:16.908 --> 36:18.074
I don't know. I, like, knew it

36:18.177 --> 36:20.104
before he stepped in the ring
and he just...

36:20.206 --> 36:21.573
What do you mean?

36:21.675 --> 36:24.709
Well, he just wasn't serious,
I think, and...

36:25.716 --> 36:26.677
About the fight.

36:26.779 --> 36:28.213
Like the past two weeks
we've been out drinking

36:28.315 --> 36:30.019
and stuff and partying and...

36:30.121 --> 36:32.117
-You never brought that up?
-To you?

36:32.219 --> 36:34.422
-To me, yeah.
-Why?

36:34.524 --> 36:36.587
He doesn't need to be drinking
two weeks before a fight.

36:36.689 --> 36:38.390
I'm not his trainer,
and I'm not a fighter.

36:38.492 --> 36:40.857
And... And he seemed
fine about it.

36:42.162 --> 36:43.493
He seemed fine.

36:43.595 --> 36:45.034
And I don't know
if he ever thought

36:45.136 --> 36:47.035
this was possible,
that he would lose.

36:47.137 --> 36:48.865
And I didn't think
it was possible.

36:49.907 --> 36:51.967
Hmm. All right. I get it.

36:53.640 --> 36:55.344
-Just be there for him. Okay?
-DAWN: Yeah.

37:02.216 --> 37:04.353
(SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING)

37:19.165 --> 37:20.336
(MARK SIGHS)

37:22.039 --> 37:23.036
(SAKAKIBARA SPEAKING JAPANESE)

37:23.138 --> 37:24.967
(CONTINUES IN JAPANESE)

37:26.377 --> 37:27.777
(IN ENGLISH) We have decided
to call this fight

37:27.879 --> 37:29.510
with Igor no contest.

37:31.815 --> 37:32.810
No contest.

37:33.378 --> 37:36.352
(SPEAKING JAPANESE)

37:36.454 --> 37:37.786
(IN ENGLISH) We would be
very happy to have you back

37:37.888 --> 37:38.855
at Pride again.

37:38.957 --> 37:40.184
-Thank you.
<i> -Arigato.</i>

37:40.286 --> 37:41.758
(SPEAKING JAPANESE)

37:41.860 --> 37:42.820
(IN ENGLISH) Thank you.

37:43.992 --> 37:44.987
What'd they say?

37:47.858 --> 37:49.864
They decided
to call it a no contest.

37:49.966 --> 37:51.728
That's awesome.

37:51.830 --> 37:53.364
That's awesome.
Why are you still so sad?

37:53.466 --> 37:55.138
Because Dawn... I'm not sad.

37:55.240 --> 37:57.369
It's just I don't do that
for no contest.

37:57.471 --> 37:59.039
-Mmm-hmm.
-I want the decision.

37:59.141 --> 38:00.108
-Mmm-hmm.
-You know?

38:00.210 --> 38:01.673
I mean, it's just
I'm out there.

38:01.775 --> 38:04.709
I'm sacrificing everything,
literally, you know.

38:04.811 --> 38:06.346
-Mmm-hmm. I see it.
-I'm sacrificing everything

38:06.448 --> 38:07.677
-out there...
-Yeah, it's very heavy.

38:07.779 --> 38:09.152
-...for the reward at the end.
-Right.

38:09.254 --> 38:11.615
It's... the high
from that thing that I do.

38:11.717 --> 38:13.151
The thing that
I just did out there.

38:13.253 --> 38:14.520
It's a high that...

38:14.623 --> 38:16.258
There's no other high
like it in the world.

38:16.360 --> 38:18.359
I can only imagine.
I... Yeah, I can see it.

38:18.461 --> 38:20.557
I can see it in you
when you're doing it,

38:20.659 --> 38:22.296
-you know?
-It's 40,000 people...

38:22.398 --> 38:23.932
-Yeah.
-...in there cheering you on.

38:24.034 --> 38:25.032
I mean, that's orgasmic.

38:25.134 --> 38:26.330
Yeah, I know... (CHUCKLES)

38:26.432 --> 38:27.936
Dawn, I'm not kidding.

38:28.038 --> 38:29.402
I'm not kidding. It's...

38:29.504 --> 38:31.667
I'm talking about
the highest of highs.

38:31.769 --> 38:34.372
-Mmm-hmm.
-And two men out there

38:34.474 --> 38:36.275
competing against each other.

38:36.378 --> 38:39.182
And it's only us
and it's so raw.

38:39.284 --> 38:40.412
-But you...
-That competition is crazy.

38:40.514 --> 38:42.184
...got to have
the competition...

38:42.286 --> 38:44.820
And you had that
feeling, you fought.

38:44.922 --> 38:45.949
You had that feeling

38:46.051 --> 38:47.816
but you don't seem...
you don't seem happy about it.

38:47.918 --> 38:50.225
No. I'm trying to
explain it to you,

38:50.327 --> 38:52.225
-but you just keep talking.
-Yeah.

38:52.327 --> 38:53.692
You just keep talking over me.

38:53.794 --> 38:55.657
No, I'm trying to understand
what you're saying

38:55.760 --> 38:57.331
and I'm trying to
support you.

38:57.433 --> 38:59.034
I know, but only
because I'm trying to

38:59.137 --> 39:00.202
tell you exactly
what happened.

39:00.304 --> 39:02.138
-IGOR: Whoa, whoa, whoa!
-(MARK CHUCKLES)

39:02.240 --> 39:03.832
-Hey, brother!
-IGOR: How you doing?

39:03.934 --> 39:05.636
-MARK: How are you? Oh.
-IGOR: Ow!

39:05.738 --> 39:08.341
MARK: Oh, you okay?
Gosh, I'm sorry.

39:08.443 --> 39:10.110
-Is that from me?
-(CHUCKLES) Yeah.

39:10.212 --> 39:11.410
Let me see. Can I see?

39:11.512 --> 39:12.778
(TRANSLATOR SPEAKING
UKRAINIAN)

39:13.917 --> 39:14.912
(IGOR GRUNTS)

39:15.014 --> 39:18.053
-Nice. How many stitches?
-(IGOR SPEAKING UKRAINIAN)

39:18.155 --> 39:19.254
TRANSLATOR: (IN ENGLISH) Four.

39:19.356 --> 39:21.156
-MARK: Four stitches.
-Four. Four.

39:21.258 --> 39:23.288
(CHUCKLES)
Does the body feel okay?

39:23.390 --> 39:24.624
(IGOR SPEAKING UKRAINIAN)

39:24.726 --> 39:26.426
TRANSLATOR: (IN ENGLISH)
A little bit of the knee.

39:26.528 --> 39:27.591
-A little bit of the knee.
-IGOR: Yeah.

39:27.693 --> 39:29.593
You know why?
A lot of my head.

39:29.695 --> 39:30.728
(TRANSLATOR SPEAKING
UKRAINIAN)

39:30.830 --> 39:32.630
-(IGOR SPEAKING UKRAINIAN)
-(MARK CHUCKLES)

39:32.732 --> 39:34.871
-I'm sorry.
-No, no, no, it's okay.

39:34.973 --> 39:36.338
Ah! It's totally okay.

39:36.440 --> 39:38.404
Tell him it's natural.
A natural reaction.

39:38.506 --> 39:40.002
(TRANSLATOR SPEAKING
UKRAINIAN)

39:40.104 --> 39:42.342
My head was down there.
My face is down there.

39:42.444 --> 39:43.878
(TRANSLATOR SPEAKING
UKRAINIAN)

39:43.980 --> 39:45.674
(ALL LAUGHING)

39:45.776 --> 39:46.877
Let's all get a picture. Yeah?

39:46.979 --> 39:48.383
IGOR: Yeah, yeah, yeah.
Let's do it together.

39:48.485 --> 39:49.613
-Let's do it. Yes. Yes.
-IGOR: Of course.

39:49.715 --> 39:51.218
-Can you do a picture?
-Come on!

39:51.320 --> 39:52.316
Let's all get in. Let's all...

39:52.418 --> 39:53.487
Everybody get in.

39:53.590 --> 39:55.156
Hey, Dawn, can you take
this picture for us?

39:55.258 --> 39:56.418
DAWN: Yeah.
MARK: Thank you.

39:56.520 --> 39:57.589
Yeah, come on.

39:57.691 --> 39:59.124
IGOR'S MANAGER:
Look at you two guys.

39:59.226 --> 40:00.430
The best ones.

40:00.532 --> 40:02.226
-Two of the best ones.
-(MARK LAUGHING) That's it.

40:02.328 --> 40:03.565
IGOR: That's it.

40:05.533 --> 40:07.864
(CAMERA SHUTTER
CLICKS, WHIRRS)

40:07.966 --> 40:09.635
-IGOR'S MANAGER: Thank you.
-Thank you.

40:09.737 --> 40:11.371
-IGOR'S MANAGER: Thank you.
-Great fight.

40:11.473 --> 40:12.736
-No, this is cold.
-MARK: Cold?

40:12.838 --> 40:14.143
PHARMACIST: Cold.
MARK: Cold and heat?

40:14.245 --> 40:15.912
-This is heat.
-MARK: Heat. Okay.

40:16.014 --> 40:17.641
Thank you. Um, three?

40:17.743 --> 40:19.014
-PHARMACIST: Three, uh...
-Yes.

40:19.116 --> 40:21.110
No, no. Just the one.

40:22.219 --> 40:24.151
-Really? Just one?
-Yeah.

40:24.253 --> 40:25.920
-Just one.
-Just one.

40:26.022 --> 40:26.949
MARK: Okay.

40:27.052 --> 40:32.127
Do you have any,
um, stronger pain medication?

40:32.230 --> 40:33.728
-Pain medication?
-MARK: Yes.

40:33.830 --> 40:35.694
Honey, I don't think they...
I don't think they do that.

40:35.797 --> 40:38.429
No, they do. They've got
everything back there.

40:38.531 --> 40:41.430
Like narcotics, opiates.

40:41.532 --> 40:43.673
No, no, no.

40:43.775 --> 40:44.500
Why not?

40:44.602 --> 40:46.135
Um, you must...

40:47.538 --> 40:48.541
Certification.

40:48.643 --> 40:51.311
-Certification? Yes. Yes.
-Yes. Yes.

40:51.413 --> 40:52.477
-Permission.
-Permission.

40:52.580 --> 40:54.042
-Yes.
-Mark, let's just go.

40:54.145 --> 40:55.713
-It's okay, he has it.
-It's okay. Just take...

40:55.815 --> 40:57.118
take what they have
and we should go.

40:57.220 --> 40:59.021
We have it. Permission.

40:59.123 --> 41:00.622
You get permission for me.

41:01.189 --> 41:02.456
Thank you.

41:02.558 --> 41:04.353
-No, no, it's too late.
-MARK: Yes.

41:04.455 --> 41:05.789
No, no.

41:05.891 --> 41:09.565
What do you have
for me that's strong?

41:10.331 --> 41:13.533
I have Advil. Advil.

41:13.635 --> 41:15.568
-Advil? (CHUCKLES)
-Advil. Yeah, yeah.

41:15.670 --> 41:18.167
-(DAWN CLEARS THROAT)
-Okay. Thank you.

41:20.142 --> 41:20.903
Thank you.

41:21.005 --> 41:22.212
-Dawn, would you like some?
-No, no.

41:22.314 --> 41:23.306
They're handing them out
like candy.

41:23.409 --> 41:24.646
Thank you.

41:32.486 --> 41:34.051
You want to hold my hand?

41:37.092 --> 41:38.088
Okay.

41:42.058 --> 41:44.600
MARK:<i> Hey, Joan.</i>
<i> Hey, it's Mark.</i>

41:45.765 --> 41:47.570
Yeah, I'm great.
How you doing?

41:48.968 --> 41:51.735
Great. I'm calling
because I know Dr. Rob

41:51.837 --> 41:53.372
was gonna write that
prescription

41:53.474 --> 41:56.040
for, um, Voltaren for me.

41:56.908 --> 41:59.611
Yeah, but Voltaren
as... as a pill,

41:59.713 --> 42:01.683
it's a little hard
on my tummy.

42:03.282 --> 42:05.884
Yeah, and I know that you guys
can give me the injection,

42:05.986 --> 42:08.723
but you don't wanna
see me in there every day.

42:09.224 --> 42:10.085
(CHUCKLING)

42:10.187 --> 42:12.592
So, what I was hoping is
if Dr. Rob can write

42:12.694 --> 42:14.160
a prescription,
that's a little better

42:14.262 --> 42:15.464
than Voltaren,

42:15.567 --> 42:18.700
um, that's a little stronger,
too, as well.

42:20.270 --> 42:22.532
Yeah. Oh, great. Yeah.

42:22.634 --> 42:23.768
That would be great.

42:23.870 --> 42:25.339
So, whenever he gets back
in the office,

42:25.441 --> 42:26.436
just have him give me a call.

42:26.538 --> 42:28.103
I'll be here.

42:28.206 --> 42:30.809
I... I'm feeling really good.
I appreciate it.

42:30.911 --> 42:33.248
Well, you know,
like a day without pain is

42:33.350 --> 42:34.543
like a day without sunshine.

42:34.645 --> 42:35.815
(CHUCKLING)

42:35.917 --> 42:38.049
<i> (RHYTHM OF MY HEART</i> PLAYING
ON CAR SPEAKERS)

42:45.460 --> 42:47.127
(PARKING BRAKE CRANKS)

42:47.229 --> 42:48.191
(MUSIC STOPS)

42:55.239 --> 42:57.200
(UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING)

43:07.781 --> 43:09.817
(SOFTLY)
Go back to sleep, okay?

43:31.972 --> 43:33.871
MAN: (ON TV)
<i> This solitary clock rotates</i>

43:33.973 --> 43:35.742
<i> six different melodies</i>
<i> on the hour.</i>

43:35.845 --> 43:38.081
<i> As the bell ringer</i>
<i> strikes the rotating...</i>

43:38.183 --> 43:39.374
(CONTINUES INDISTINCTLY)

43:40.580 --> 43:41.981
(UTENSILS CLUNKING)

43:43.816 --> 43:44.913
<i> You're the first bidder...</i>

43:45.015 --> 43:46.255
(INDISTINCT CLAMORING ON TV)

43:46.357 --> 43:47.723
You gotta keep eating, Mark.

43:48.289 --> 43:49.689
Yeah.

43:49.791 --> 43:50.787
-DAWN: You're not gonna get...
-I will.

43:50.889 --> 43:52.425
...any better unless you eat.

43:52.527 --> 43:54.593
-Yeah.
-(FORK CLANKS)

43:54.696 --> 43:56.599
-I know.
-I can't keep coming out

43:56.701 --> 43:58.998
and finding you
like this, Mark. It's just...

44:01.238 --> 44:01.998
What do you mean?

44:02.100 --> 44:03.370
You keep telling me
you're gonna quit

44:03.472 --> 44:05.034
and then I come out and...

44:05.136 --> 44:07.038
Baby, I just need to,
you know...

44:07.140 --> 44:10.646
I just have to get through
this... this moment.

44:10.748 --> 44:12.275
-You know, it's fine.
-What do you want from me?

44:12.377 --> 44:14.282
Do you want me just to pretend
that everything's fine?

44:14.384 --> 44:15.482
No. What do you mean?

44:15.584 --> 44:16.785
That you don't look like this?

44:16.887 --> 44:18.182
I don't look like...
I just want you to be my girl.

44:18.284 --> 44:21.284
That's all. What do you mean?
Look like what? (MUMBLES)

44:23.421 --> 44:26.761
DAWN: You keep telling me
we're going to take a hike.

44:26.863 --> 44:29.193
We are gonna take a hike.
We're going to go today.

44:35.232 --> 44:37.098
You don't even hide it
from me anymore.

44:37.200 --> 44:38.538
I keep going
into the bathroom,

44:38.640 --> 44:39.605
seeing your shit everywhere.

44:39.708 --> 44:40.806
-It's okay.
-It's not okay.

44:40.908 --> 44:42.303
-It's okay.
-It's getting bad, Mark.

44:42.406 --> 44:43.908
-No, it's for pain.
-This is getting crazy.

44:44.010 --> 44:46.075
-That's for pain.
-No. No, it's insane.

44:46.177 --> 44:47.911
And you need to get
serious now, okay?

44:48.013 --> 44:49.246
I am serious.
What do you mean?

44:49.348 --> 44:50.486
Because I don't even know
who this person is right now.

44:50.588 --> 44:51.486
I'm ser...
I'm going through this.

44:51.588 --> 44:52.848
What... Going through
the house

44:52.950 --> 44:53.951
looking to find stuff

44:54.053 --> 44:55.417
-just to get me into trouble?
-No.

44:55.519 --> 44:56.955
How about you stop treating me
like a fucking child?

44:57.057 --> 44:58.723
-How about that?
-How about you stop acting

44:58.825 --> 44:59.988
like one, I wouldn't have to.

45:00.090 --> 45:02.331
Like you... You lost a fight.

45:02.433 --> 45:05.095
Big deal. Just get over it.

45:05.198 --> 45:07.396
(MAN ON TV CONTINUES SPEAKING
INDISTINCTLY)

45:28.522 --> 45:29.484
(BLOWS THUDDING)

46:11.666 --> 46:12.794
(ICE DISPENSER CLICKS)

46:12.896 --> 46:15.101
(ICE CLATTERING)

46:27.949 --> 46:29.852
I just need you to
treat me like a man.

46:30.485 --> 46:31.821
(SNIFFLES)

46:50.000 --> 46:51.302
DAWN: I love you.

46:53.106 --> 46:55.570
You're my big strong man.
I love you.

46:56.807 --> 46:58.012
Okay?

47:07.587 --> 47:09.155
(SOBBING)

47:15.862 --> 47:17.128
COLEMAN: You wanna fight?

47:17.230 --> 47:20.835
I'll take that. Let's go.
(IMITATES YELLING)

47:20.937 --> 47:22.898
You ready?
Okay, let's see what you got.

47:23.000 --> 47:24.866
(IMITATES GRUNTING)

47:24.968 --> 47:26.738
(BABY CRYING)

47:26.840 --> 47:28.707
Looks like I'm winning.

47:28.809 --> 47:29.971
KELLEY: Okay, okay, okay.

47:30.073 --> 47:31.974
The winner is Daddy!

47:32.076 --> 47:33.242
(BABY CONTINUES CRYING)

47:33.344 --> 47:35.651
Fought a tough opponent.
My toughest yet.

47:35.753 --> 47:38.013
Feels good to be
in the win column again.

47:38.115 --> 47:39.751
And after this payday,

47:39.853 --> 47:41.889
I'm gonna get my girl

47:41.992 --> 47:44.861
-a new playhouse, and a bike.
-(PHONE RINGING)

47:45.660 --> 47:47.226
And... Hold on.

47:48.599 --> 47:50.026
(INDISTINCT CHATTERING ON TV)

47:50.128 --> 47:51.664
-(KELLEY SHUSHING)
-Hello.

47:51.766 --> 47:53.000
(DAWN SOBBING ON PHONE)

47:53.102 --> 47:55.636
He's laying on the ground
and he wouldn't wake up

47:55.738 --> 47:57.170
and I couldn't move him and...

47:57.272 --> 47:58.401
<i> -I was like shaking him...</i>
-(WHISPERING) It's Dawn.

47:58.503 --> 47:59.909
-DAWN:<i> ...and he's like...</i>
-She's freaking out.

48:00.011 --> 48:02.042
DAWN:<i> ...took too much</i>
<i> or something.</i> (SOBBING)

48:02.144 --> 48:04.611
Walk me through everything
from the beginning.

48:04.713 --> 48:05.944
I think he did too much

48:06.046 --> 48:07.383
and then I couldn't
wake him up.

48:07.485 --> 48:08.377
I found him on the ground

48:08.480 --> 48:11.220
and then I just was like
shaking him and stuff.

48:11.322 --> 48:12.449
Is he alive?

48:12.551 --> 48:15.789
He's alive, but I didn't know,
you know, at first.

48:15.891 --> 48:17.955
Oh, my fucking God.
Okay. Um...

48:18.057 --> 48:19.792
(DAWN SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY)

48:19.894 --> 48:20.994
I know. Calm down, calm down.

48:21.097 --> 48:23.292
Okay. I need you to
come and help me, okay?

48:23.394 --> 48:25.062
I'm gonna get
on the first flight out.

48:25.164 --> 48:27.295
All right?
I'm going to help you.

48:27.397 --> 48:29.265
I will be there
as soon as I can.

48:29.367 --> 48:30.769
DAWN:<i> I need you to</i>
<i> talk to him.</i>

48:30.871 --> 48:32.200
I got you. I got you.

48:32.302 --> 48:33.235
(DAWN SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY)

48:33.337 --> 48:35.975
I'll see you soon.
First flight.

48:36.077 --> 48:38.013
-DAWN:<i> Okay.</i>
-All right. Bye, Dawn.

48:39.948 --> 48:42.116
(INDISTINCT ANNOUNCEMENT
ON PA)

48:45.184 --> 48:47.083
Sorry. Where's
Mark Kerr's room?

48:47.185 --> 48:48.390
Oh. Right down the hall, sir.

48:48.492 --> 48:49.590
COLEMAN: Thank you.

48:49.692 --> 48:51.653
(INDISTINCT CHATTERING)

48:53.322 --> 48:54.656
-Coleman.
-COLEMAN: Hey.

48:56.994 --> 48:57.996
(SOFTLY) I know.

48:58.098 --> 49:00.266
-I know, I know.
-(DAWN SOBBING)

49:01.300 --> 49:03.200
-How's he doing?
-DAWN: He just woke up.

49:03.302 --> 49:06.037
He's like in and out
and he's not okay.

49:06.139 --> 49:07.303
-He's awake though?
-DAWN: Yeah.

49:07.405 --> 49:09.077
-You care if I go in?
-DAWN: Yeah.

49:18.016 --> 49:19.186
(KNOCKING ON DOOR)

49:21.825 --> 49:22.791
COLEMAN: What's
going on, buddy?

49:22.893 --> 49:24.994
-MARK: Hey. (CHUCKLES)
-How are you?

49:25.991 --> 49:27.863
What's up, Coleman?

49:27.966 --> 49:30.492
You're a sight for sore eyes.
Jesus chrimey!

49:30.595 --> 49:32.760
You're looking a little rough.
Not gonna lie.

49:32.862 --> 49:36.234
Oh, man. You should see
the soap in this place, man.

49:36.336 --> 49:38.301
-COLEMAN: Is it bad?
-It's like fucking glue.

49:38.403 --> 49:40.804
-(LAUGHS) Yeah.
-I can kind of see it.

49:40.906 --> 49:41.943
I know, man.

49:42.045 --> 49:43.705
It's doing a number
on my hair, you know.

49:44.415 --> 49:45.209
Yeah, yeah.

49:45.311 --> 49:47.782
-Man, you look good, man.
-Thank you.

49:47.884 --> 49:50.181
So, uh,
what the fuck happened?

49:50.283 --> 49:52.648
-Oh, man.
-You get sick or something?

49:53.591 --> 49:56.685
Yeah. I, um, got sick.

49:56.787 --> 50:00.396
I got sick and it was...
it was pretty unbelievable.

50:00.498 --> 50:01.797
It was pretty bad.

50:01.899 --> 50:04.565
That's the right word.
"It" was bad.

50:04.667 --> 50:06.035
-Mmm-hmm.
-Yeah.

50:06.436 --> 50:07.432
Um...

50:08.970 --> 50:10.673
-Yeah.
-So what happened?

50:10.775 --> 50:12.107
Can you give me
the whole story?

50:12.575 --> 50:13.536
Um, I was...

50:13.638 --> 50:17.541
I was on the floor
and... and I couldn't wake up.

50:18.648 --> 50:20.216
And then I, um...

50:21.019 --> 50:22.850
And then Dawn came in
and she was trying to

50:22.952 --> 50:24.513
wake me up
and... she couldn't...

50:24.615 --> 50:26.715
She couldn't wake me up
either and, um...

50:28.524 --> 50:29.520
Um...

50:30.725 --> 50:31.687
You're good.

50:32.155 --> 50:33.394
That's weird.

50:33.497 --> 50:35.062
It's fine.

50:35.165 --> 50:36.791
-Keep going though.
-Yeah, yeah. You know me.

50:36.893 --> 50:39.233
-I don't have verbal pauses.
-I know that. I know that.

50:40.063 --> 50:41.131
Um...

50:41.233 --> 50:43.699
So, then Dawn called the...

50:44.542 --> 50:45.806
She called 911.

50:45.908 --> 50:48.042
And then the ambulance came,

50:48.145 --> 50:50.545
the paramedics came in
and then they couldn't

50:50.647 --> 50:51.773
wake me up either.

50:53.445 --> 50:55.076
And then they put me
in the ambulance

50:55.178 --> 50:56.711
and then they...

50:56.813 --> 50:59.348
I was kind of like
in this weird, altered state.

50:59.450 --> 51:01.287
Like, I was aware of
where I was,

51:01.389 --> 51:03.252
and I could kind of
see things a little blurred,

51:03.354 --> 51:04.992
but I could hear everything.

51:05.094 --> 51:07.355
So my acuity was...
was pretty good.

51:07.457 --> 51:09.965
They were asking me questions,

51:10.067 --> 51:11.796
and... I got a few of
the questions wrong

51:11.898 --> 51:13.130
a little bit.

51:13.232 --> 51:14.397
Like who was the president.

51:14.499 --> 51:15.801
They said,
"Who is the president?"

51:15.903 --> 51:17.098
What'd you say?

51:17.200 --> 51:18.401
Ronald Reagan.

51:18.503 --> 51:20.701
(LAUGHING)
You fucking believe that?

51:20.804 --> 51:22.944
I mean, shit,
you'd say that anyway, right?

51:23.046 --> 51:24.608
I would say that
even on a good day,

51:24.710 --> 51:27.512
I was telling them, like,
"You guys can't ask that."

51:27.614 --> 51:30.147
That's when I realized, like,
that's kind of unfair,

51:30.249 --> 51:31.883
you know, the way they were...

51:31.985 --> 51:33.080
-Hey.
-Yeah.

51:33.182 --> 51:34.723
Listen.

51:34.825 --> 51:37.291
Just stop, all right? Please?

51:40.390 --> 51:41.559
COLEMAN: Hey, you're good.

51:42.533 --> 51:43.661
(MARK SOBBING)

51:43.763 --> 51:48.062
Look. I didn't come out here
because I love Phoenix, dude.

51:48.165 --> 51:49.435
All right?

51:51.141 --> 51:52.939
I came out here
because I want to see you

51:53.042 --> 51:55.339
-get better.
-(MARK SOBBING)

51:55.441 --> 51:58.306
You can't keep doing this
to yourself.

51:58.408 --> 52:00.011
MARK: I know. (SNIFFLES)

52:00.113 --> 52:01.344
-I'm so sorry.
-It's me.

52:01.446 --> 52:04.383
You don't have to
apologize, okay?

52:04.485 --> 52:07.016
I'm one of your best friends
in the world, right?

52:07.118 --> 52:08.221
MARK: Yeah.

52:08.323 --> 52:10.487
COLEMAN: And I'm here
because I love you.

52:10.590 --> 52:13.294
-(SOBBING) I love you, too.
-Okay, come here.

52:13.995 --> 52:15.593
Come here. Come here.

52:17.330 --> 52:18.995
-Yeah.
-I fucking love you, man.

52:19.097 --> 52:21.269
(MARK SOBBING)

52:24.872 --> 52:26.208
I'm sorry.

52:26.875 --> 52:28.308
I don't wanna die.

52:28.410 --> 52:31.280
COLEMAN: Hey, look at me.
You're not gonna die.

52:31.749 --> 52:32.779
All right? Look at me.

52:32.881 --> 52:34.213
I can't. I can't.

52:34.315 --> 52:36.149
We're all in this
together, all right?

52:36.251 --> 52:38.385
There's tons of people
that love you.

52:39.452 --> 52:41.249
But it's got to start
with you, okay?

52:41.351 --> 52:42.686
And you got this.

52:43.825 --> 52:45.224
All right?

52:45.326 --> 52:47.625
All right. I know.
I know. (SNIFFLES)

52:48.763 --> 52:49.726
I know.

52:50.865 --> 52:51.827
Thank you.

52:54.401 --> 52:56.601
<i> (DON'T BE CRUEL</i>
BY BILLY SWAN PLAYING)

54:12.212 --> 54:13.412
(INDISTINCT CHATTERING)

54:13.514 --> 54:14.877
-That's it?
-PHOTOGRAPHER: Thanks so much.

54:17.152 --> 54:18.852
Thank you for having me today.

54:18.954 --> 54:19.847
COLEMAN: No problem.

54:19.950 --> 54:23.017
I have a little bit
strange question for you.

54:23.660 --> 54:24.522
Okay.

54:24.625 --> 54:28.363
Um, are you okay
to fight without your friend?

54:29.263 --> 54:31.659
-Mark Kerr?
-Yes, Mark Kerr.

54:31.761 --> 54:33.131
Yeah, I've been
worried about him

54:33.233 --> 54:35.332
for quite a while now.

54:35.434 --> 54:37.201
You know, just as a friend.

54:37.303 --> 54:39.071
Yeah, I know your feeling.

54:39.173 --> 54:41.309
I think that loss to Igor,

54:41.411 --> 54:43.672
or whatever you wanna call it,
the no contest.

54:43.774 --> 54:45.209
I think that was
the best thing that

54:45.311 --> 54:46.711
could've happened to him.

54:46.813 --> 54:49.312
I feel like he's going
to come back a better version

54:49.414 --> 54:50.645
of himself, you know.

54:50.747 --> 54:51.984
And I know he wants
to be here.

54:52.086 --> 54:53.550
He loves you guys.

54:53.652 --> 54:56.091
And he's distraught that
he can't make it.

54:56.193 --> 54:59.657
So, what make you
keeping motivated?

54:59.759 --> 55:02.424
I mean, a lot of people
tell me I should retire.

55:02.526 --> 55:03.998
You know, and give it up.

55:04.100 --> 55:06.902
But I got a family, you know.

55:07.004 --> 55:09.698
And there's a lot worse ways

55:09.800 --> 55:12.140
<i> to make a living,</i>
<i> you know, so...</i>

55:12.242 --> 55:15.440
<i> Um, I'm looking forward</i>
<i> to Sunday.</i>

55:15.542 --> 55:17.775
<i> I think it's gonna be</i>
<i> a good one.</i>

55:17.877 --> 55:19.743
STEPHEN QUADROS:<i> So not only</i>
<i> is Mark Coleman here</i>

55:19.845 --> 55:22.284
<i> without the support of</i>
<i> his friend Mark Kerr,</i>

55:22.386 --> 55:23.914
<i> who had to drop out</i>
<i> of his own fight here</i>

55:24.016 --> 55:25.517
<i> -due to health reasons...</i>
-(MEN YELLING INDISTINCTLY)

55:25.619 --> 55:28.152
<i> ...but he is also</i>
<i> on an uphill battle</i>

55:28.254 --> 55:29.523
<i> against time.</i>

55:29.625 --> 55:32.955
<i> After his recent losses,</i>
<i> you have to ask yourself,</i>

55:33.057 --> 55:35.793
<i> "Is this the end of the road</i>
<i> for Mark Coleman?</i>

55:35.895 --> 55:40.369
<i> "Or will he extend his career</i>
<i> just one more time?"</i>

55:40.471 --> 55:42.668
MAN 1: Turn him around.
But don't strike with him.

55:43.202 --> 55:44.406
That's it!

55:46.309 --> 55:47.570
MAN 2: Going good.
MAN 1: Don't strike.

55:47.672 --> 55:48.669
MAN 2: Now!
Shoot, shoot, shoot!

55:48.772 --> 55:50.376
MAN 1:
Shoot! Take him down!

55:50.478 --> 55:52.005
Yeah! That's what
I'm talking about!

55:52.108 --> 55:54.212
MAN 2: You got him.
MAN 3: Smash him, Thor!

55:54.314 --> 55:55.282
MAN 4: Tear him down!

55:55.384 --> 55:56.983
MAN 1: Pound him!
Pound him! Come on.

55:57.085 --> 55:58.112
Pass the guard!

55:58.214 --> 56:00.388
-Come on, pass that guard.
-MAN 2: Add the pressure.

56:00.490 --> 56:02.518
MAN 5: Hit him! Yes!
MAN 6: There we go! Come on!

56:02.620 --> 56:04.152
MAN 1: Come on! Hit him again.

56:04.487 --> 56:05.721
Pass that guard!

56:05.823 --> 56:07.325
MAN 2: That's it, that's it,
that's it.

56:07.427 --> 56:08.829
MAN 1: Come on! Don't stop!

56:08.931 --> 56:09.726
Don't stop!

56:09.828 --> 56:11.694
-MAN 3: That's it! Yes!
-(BELL RINGING)

56:11.796 --> 56:13.334
STEPHEN QUADROS:
<i> Coleman has done it!</i>

56:13.436 --> 56:15.838
<i> He has won here</i>
<i> at Pride 8 championship</i>

56:15.940 --> 56:16.897
<i> over Ricardo Morais,</i>

56:16.999 --> 56:19.868
<i> breathing new life</i>
<i> into his career.</i>

56:19.970 --> 56:21.804
<i> He clearly has worked</i>
<i> long and hard</i>

56:21.906 --> 56:25.177
<i> to get back in this place</i>
<i> and mindset.</i>

56:25.279 --> 56:27.548
(AUTOMATED GATE WHIRRING)

56:35.886 --> 56:37.654
MARK: Never looked
more beautiful.

56:37.756 --> 56:40.022
DAWN: You look
so beautiful, baby.

56:42.363 --> 56:44.328
I missed you so much, baby.

56:44.430 --> 56:46.633
(UPLIFTING MUSIC PLAYING)

56:55.572 --> 56:57.743
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

57:00.182 --> 57:02.176
(SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY)

57:08.322 --> 57:10.092
MARK: (LAUGHS) Come on!

57:10.194 --> 57:13.462
DAWN: Mmm.
The Gravitron! Look!

57:14.428 --> 57:16.465
I love the Gravitron. So good.

57:18.033 --> 57:19.301
-No?
-Well...

57:19.403 --> 57:21.437
Let's do it. Let's do it.
This is the best.

57:23.471 --> 57:25.005
There's no way
I can ride that.

57:25.107 --> 57:26.205
DAWN: Why? Why?

57:26.307 --> 57:27.441
Why? Because of my tummy.

57:27.543 --> 57:28.637
You know what that
would do to my tummy.

57:28.739 --> 57:29.978
I would get sick everywhere.

57:30.080 --> 57:31.377
-I can't do that.
-No, no.

57:31.479 --> 57:34.043
No, it's about
perspective, okay?

57:35.417 --> 57:37.481
On the inside,
you don't feel it.

57:37.583 --> 57:38.782
It's like you're not moving.

57:38.885 --> 57:41.455
You're, like,
pinned against the wall and...

57:41.558 --> 57:42.986
You're gonna love it.
You're gonna love it.

57:45.822 --> 57:46.920
Does it move on the inside?

57:47.022 --> 57:49.790
It moves,
but it's moving so fast

57:49.892 --> 57:51.632
that you can't even feel it.

57:53.570 --> 57:55.434
Hey, I really wanna go
on the ride with her,

57:55.536 --> 57:57.137
but I have
a sensitive stomach.

57:57.239 --> 57:58.633
Is there... Is there...

57:58.735 --> 58:00.001
The center part in there,

58:00.103 --> 58:01.904
that's the thing that
stays still, right?

58:02.006 --> 58:03.640
Can I stand in there?
In the middle part?

58:03.742 --> 58:05.139
-In the center part?
-MARK: Yes.

58:05.241 --> 58:07.779
No, man, that would be
a serious liability issue.

58:07.881 --> 58:10.011
Uh, well, where would you
recommend I stand then?

58:10.113 --> 58:11.581
'Cause I don't wanna
get sick on the ride,

58:11.683 --> 58:12.980
but I do wanna ride with her.

58:13.082 --> 58:14.322
You don't wanna
get sick on the ride?

58:14.424 --> 58:16.486
I would suggest
you don't go on the ride

58:16.588 --> 58:17.688
if you can't handle it.

58:17.790 --> 58:18.887
Well, it's not that
I can't handle it,

58:18.989 --> 58:20.360
it's just I'm choosing
not to go on it.

58:20.462 --> 58:21.722
Okay, I'm gonna
go on the ride.

58:21.824 --> 58:22.858
You're gonna hold my cake.

58:22.960 --> 58:24.793
-You can hold my bag.
-MARK: Okay.

58:24.895 --> 58:26.564
-Okay? Wish me luck.
-MARK: Okay.

58:26.666 --> 58:27.897
-Okay. Thank you.
-MARK: Have fun.

58:27.999 --> 58:30.033
<i> (JUST ANOTHER DAY</i>
BY JON SECADA PLAYING)

58:36.243 --> 58:37.645
(BELL RINGING)

58:39.478 --> 58:41.649
(GRAVITRON WHIRRING)

58:44.922 --> 58:45.917
(THUDDING)

58:54.896 --> 58:57.060
<i> (JUST ANOTHER DAY</i>
BY JON SECADA PLAYING LOUDLY)

59:01.401 --> 59:03.572
(IMPERCEPTIBLE)

59:07.341 --> 59:09.545
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

59:27.724 --> 59:29.895
(IMPERCEPTIBLE)

59:34.534 --> 59:36.704
(CHEERFUL MUSIC PLAYING)

59:38.640 --> 59:40.470
-MARK: Here I come!
-You look so cool!

59:40.572 --> 59:41.637
You look so cool!

59:41.739 --> 59:43.609
MARK: I feel so cool.

59:43.711 --> 59:45.310
-This is my speed, baby.
-DAWN: Okay.

59:45.412 --> 59:46.675
This is my speed.

59:46.777 --> 59:48.947
(CHEERFUL MUSIC CONTINUES)

59:50.749 --> 59:54.950
COMMENTATOR:<i> Let's go, Rambo!</i>

59:55.052 --> 59:57.758
<i> The drivers are</i>
<i> circling together.</i>

59:58.259 --> 01:00:00.759
Come on, 45!

01:00:00.862 --> 01:00:03.925
COMMENTATOR:<i> Andy Garcia is</i>
<i> still in this.</i>

01:00:04.027 --> 01:00:06.800
-Oh!
-COMMENTATOR:<i> Andy Garcia!</i>

01:00:08.138 --> 01:00:09.770
<i> Here comes...</i>

01:00:10.270 --> 01:00:11.640
ALL: Oh!

01:00:12.506 --> 01:00:13.703
(PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING)

01:00:13.806 --> 01:00:15.605
-Oh!
-COMMENTATOR:<i> Great hit!</i>

01:00:15.707 --> 01:00:17.710
<i> Not giving up just yet.</i>

01:00:17.812 --> 01:00:20.242
<i> Oh, I think that</i>
<i> back wheel has had it.</i>

01:00:21.018 --> 01:00:21.944
DAWN: Yes!

01:00:22.046 --> 01:00:23.178
COMMENTATOR:<i> He's good.</i>
<i> He's gotta</i>

01:00:23.280 --> 01:00:25.418
<i> find a way out of this,</i>
<i> because they just keep</i>

01:00:25.521 --> 01:00:27.148
<i> hitting him in the same spot.</i>

01:00:27.250 --> 01:00:30.186
-Whoo-hoo!
-COMMENTATOR:<i> Oh, here we go!</i>

01:00:31.724 --> 01:00:33.759
<i> Oh, getting flattened now!</i>

01:00:33.861 --> 01:00:36.598
<i> Full speed ahead!</i>
<i> Full speed ahead!</i>

01:00:36.700 --> 01:00:39.267
-(SENTIMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING)
-COMMENTATOR:<i> Oh!</i>

01:00:39.370 --> 01:00:42.000
<i> Madden does another hard hit.</i>

01:00:42.832 --> 01:00:44.099
<i> Checking on 50.</i>

01:00:44.202 --> 01:00:47.406
<i> The Kenney boys are still</i>
<i> in the mix here</i>

01:00:47.508 --> 01:00:48.509
<i> and still moving around.</i>

01:00:48.611 --> 01:00:51.077
-(CONTINUES INDISTINCTLY)
-He's okay!

01:00:51.180 --> 01:00:52.180
(CLAPPING)

01:00:52.282 --> 01:00:54.209
-Whoo!
-He's okay!

01:00:54.311 --> 01:00:56.784
COMMENTATOR:<i> Rick's car is</i>
<i> hit the hardest...</i>

01:01:10.294 --> 01:01:12.764
MARK: Dawn, what happened
with this over here?

01:01:12.866 --> 01:01:13.931
-What do you mean?
-I asked you to

01:01:14.033 --> 01:01:16.968
prune the bottom
so the tops will get bigger.

01:01:17.070 --> 01:01:19.103
I wanted this to look like
the Road Runner cartoon.

01:01:19.205 --> 01:01:21.706
It's just a little nub
of a thing. Just cut it off.

01:01:21.808 --> 01:01:22.838
Well, that's not
the way it works.

01:01:22.940 --> 01:01:24.005
Right now, it steals water,

01:01:24.107 --> 01:01:25.477
and then it ruins
the integrity

01:01:25.579 --> 01:01:26.743
from the larger arms.

01:01:26.846 --> 01:01:27.809
Well, I'm sorry.
I didn't realize

01:01:27.911 --> 01:01:28.946
it was such a big deal.

01:01:29.048 --> 01:01:31.586
It's just...
It's just a plant. (LAUGHS)

01:01:31.689 --> 01:01:34.048
It's not just a plant.
That's a saguaro cactus.

01:01:34.150 --> 01:01:35.757
They're hard
to grow like that.

01:01:36.953 --> 01:01:38.188
Can I have that knife?

01:02:17.798 --> 01:02:19.100
You'd make
a really great father,

01:02:19.202 --> 01:02:20.428
you know that?

01:02:20.530 --> 01:02:24.434
That's very nice of you
to say and I mean it, but...

01:02:24.537 --> 01:02:25.705
It's true.

01:02:25.807 --> 01:02:27.907
Well, thank you,
but I'm just not ready,

01:02:28.009 --> 01:02:29.237
and I don't know why
you keep bringing that up,

01:02:29.339 --> 01:02:31.579
by the way.
It's like you keep forcing it.

01:02:31.681 --> 01:02:33.012
I'm not forcing it.
I was just saying,

01:02:33.114 --> 01:02:34.742
you have great qualities
and you'd make a great dad,

01:02:34.844 --> 01:02:35.814
that's all.

01:02:35.916 --> 01:02:38.116
-Why'd you bring it up?
-To be nice.

01:02:38.717 --> 01:02:39.718
Well, it's not nice,

01:02:39.820 --> 01:02:41.688
because you keep
making me say no.

01:02:41.790 --> 01:02:42.916
You already know
how I feel about that.

01:02:43.018 --> 01:02:44.353
Look, I love kids...

01:02:45.188 --> 01:02:47.488
(SIGHS)
...but I'm always gone,

01:02:48.992 --> 01:02:49.993
my mind is preoccupied

01:02:50.095 --> 01:02:51.458
with everything else
that's going on,

01:02:51.560 --> 01:02:54.099
and you keep bringing this up
about having kids.

01:02:55.234 --> 01:02:56.533
I mean, I don't know
what you want me to do.

01:02:56.635 --> 01:02:57.605
I look around.

01:02:57.707 --> 01:02:58.969
I'm already doing
everything already.

01:02:59.071 --> 01:03:00.840
-That's not true, Mark.
-It is true.

01:03:00.942 --> 01:03:03.410
I'm already doing
everything around here.

01:03:03.512 --> 01:03:04.479
You don't understand.

01:03:04.581 --> 01:03:05.580
I just don't have
the mental space

01:03:05.682 --> 01:03:07.811
to have a kid.
And... And I'm sorry.

01:03:07.913 --> 01:03:09.417
I don't like telling you no.

01:03:09.519 --> 01:03:11.814
I was just trying to be nice.

01:03:11.916 --> 01:03:13.386
-I know, I know.
-Okay.

01:03:13.488 --> 01:03:15.649
And it's very nice.

01:03:15.751 --> 01:03:18.587
And... And I appreciate it.
It's just not the right time.

01:03:18.689 --> 01:03:19.861
Okay.

01:03:30.600 --> 01:03:32.434
Really, Dawn? Look at
all the leaves in the pool.

01:03:32.536 --> 01:03:35.910
Are you kidding me, Mark?
It's... That was this morning.

01:03:36.807 --> 01:03:37.978
I know, but...

01:03:39.348 --> 01:03:40.310
I'll do it.

01:03:44.817 --> 01:03:46.987
(GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING)

01:03:56.959 --> 01:03:59.164
(BIRDS CHIRPING)

01:04:06.574 --> 01:04:07.740
So, how has it been?

01:04:07.842 --> 01:04:09.039
It's been really
fucking annoying,

01:04:09.141 --> 01:04:11.679
to be honest with you.
It's just...

01:04:11.781 --> 01:04:12.976
He's on this
whole high-horse schtick

01:04:13.078 --> 01:04:14.278
and I thought
I could handle it,

01:04:14.380 --> 01:04:15.949
and I don't know if I can,
because it's like being

01:04:16.051 --> 01:04:17.983
with a completely different
fucking person now.

01:04:18.085 --> 01:04:19.554
You know how it is
when people get sober,

01:04:19.656 --> 01:04:20.989
it's all they can
talk about, so...

01:04:21.091 --> 01:04:23.490
(SCOFFS) When he was using,
he was like tender and sweet

01:04:23.592 --> 01:04:24.691
and he relied upon me,

01:04:24.793 --> 01:04:27.660
and now it's like
he's distant.

01:04:27.762 --> 01:04:29.259
It's hard, it's hard to know,

01:04:29.361 --> 01:04:31.328
and he's like shitty,
and picking on me, and...

01:04:32.094 --> 01:04:33.902
(SIGHS) Well...

01:04:35.004 --> 01:04:37.805
I think I miss
taking care of him, you know.

01:04:37.907 --> 01:04:40.070
-JACQUELINE: Yeah.
-Oh, my God. Oh, my God.

01:04:40.172 --> 01:04:41.908
-What? Oh, brain freeze?
-(EXCLAIMING)

01:04:42.010 --> 01:04:43.105
Put your tongue
on the roof of your mouth.

01:04:43.207 --> 01:04:46.012
-Mmm-mmm.
-It does. Yeah. It works.

01:04:46.114 --> 01:04:47.277
-You gotta warm it up.
-It never works. Never.

01:04:47.379 --> 01:04:49.349
-I don't know what to do.
-Okay. Here, chug this.

01:04:49.451 --> 01:04:50.446
Oh, my God.

01:04:50.981 --> 01:04:52.017
JACQUELINE: Okay.

01:04:52.119 --> 01:04:55.522
SERVER AND DAWN:
♪<i> Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

01:04:55.624 --> 01:04:59.760
♪<i> Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

01:04:59.862 --> 01:05:04.762
♪<i> Happy birthday,</i>
<i> dear Jacqueline♪</i>

01:05:04.864 --> 01:05:08.203
♪<i> Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

01:05:08.305 --> 01:05:09.097
(CHUCKLING)

01:05:09.199 --> 01:05:10.672
Thank you. I fuckin' hate you.

01:05:10.774 --> 01:05:12.136
-(DAWN CACKLING)
-I'm gonna kill you.

01:05:12.239 --> 01:05:15.038
SERVER: Enjoy.
DAWN AND JAQUELINE: Thank you!

01:05:15.140 --> 01:05:16.206
DAWN: Just remind me
never to go

01:05:16.309 --> 01:05:19.679
back to that place.
That place was the worst.

01:05:19.781 --> 01:05:22.247
I feel like I need that pizza.

01:05:39.731 --> 01:05:40.694
Sorry.

01:05:48.677 --> 01:05:50.811
-Four. Wow.
-Yep.

01:05:50.913 --> 01:05:52.238
It's a guarantee
I won't get a headache,

01:05:52.340 --> 01:05:53.707
and I can kind of feel it.

01:05:55.510 --> 01:05:57.182
Yep. That makes
a lot of sense.

01:05:57.284 --> 01:05:59.185
DAWN: Yeah, I thought so.
That's why I said it.

01:06:03.453 --> 01:06:05.485
You know,
I'm just out of rehab, Dawn.

01:06:05.587 --> 01:06:07.421
-Oh, please. Really?
-I mean, come on.

01:06:07.523 --> 01:06:09.130
It's like, I didn't do it
in front of you.

01:06:09.232 --> 01:06:11.599
I know, but you're just not
being nice to me right now.

01:06:11.702 --> 01:06:13.132
You're not being
very nice to me.

01:06:13.234 --> 01:06:14.363
What does that even mean?
I didn't do anything.

01:06:14.466 --> 01:06:15.496
-No, you're just...
-I haven't done anything.

01:06:15.598 --> 01:06:17.068
...kind of judgy,
and, like, you just got

01:06:17.170 --> 01:06:19.808
your shit together
for 21 days, like...

01:06:19.910 --> 01:06:22.239
It doesn't make you
any better than me.

01:06:22.341 --> 01:06:24.609
I'm sorry. I didn't mean it
in that way.

01:06:24.711 --> 01:06:25.772
Mark. It's...

01:06:25.874 --> 01:06:28.080
It's just 'cause you've got
a problem with something,

01:06:28.182 --> 01:06:29.212
it doesn't mean that
everyone in the world

01:06:29.314 --> 01:06:30.611
has the same problem
that you do. Okay?

01:06:30.713 --> 01:06:33.219
-So just give me a break.
-You wouldn't understand.

01:06:34.953 --> 01:06:36.123
Who are you calling?

01:06:36.890 --> 01:06:37.991
(MARK EXHALES DEEPLY)

01:06:38.094 --> 01:06:39.154
-JEFF: (ON PHONE)<i> Hello.</i>
-Hey, Jeff, it's me.

01:06:39.256 --> 01:06:40.223
Oh, it's your sponsor. Okay.

01:06:40.325 --> 01:06:42.024
You know what?
You're no fun anymore.

01:06:42.126 --> 01:06:43.260
You're no fun anymore.

01:06:43.363 --> 01:06:44.626
And you're just
a fucking tattletale bitch.

01:06:44.728 --> 01:06:45.999
-Hold on. Hold on one second.
-Are you telling on me?

01:06:46.101 --> 01:06:47.265
-I'm not telling on you.
-What are you doing?

01:06:47.367 --> 01:06:48.397
This is the most difficult
time of my life, Dawn.

01:06:48.499 --> 01:06:50.604
Please, please.
I need you to understand.

01:06:50.706 --> 01:06:51.803
-I do understand.
-Please.

01:06:51.905 --> 01:06:53.471
No, I do. I understand.

01:06:53.573 --> 01:06:55.842
But then you go and call Jeff,
and then you just shut me out.

01:06:55.944 --> 01:06:57.108
And it really hurts
my feelings,

01:06:57.210 --> 01:06:58.574
and I'm here
to talk to you, okay?

01:06:58.676 --> 01:07:00.580
But you just gotta let me in.
You don't need Jeff.

01:07:00.682 --> 01:07:01.716
Hang up. Hang up.

01:07:01.818 --> 01:07:02.880
This is what
I'm talking about.

01:07:02.982 --> 01:07:04.180
I mean, this up and down.

01:07:04.282 --> 01:07:05.653
I don't know
who I'm talking to.

01:07:05.755 --> 01:07:06.780
How the fuck can you say that?

01:07:06.882 --> 01:07:08.752
Your behavior is just
so unhealthy for me right now.

01:07:08.854 --> 01:07:10.383
Please, Dawn.

01:07:10.485 --> 01:07:12.292
You know what? Fuck you, Mark.

01:07:12.761 --> 01:07:14.293
Just go fuck yourself.

01:07:15.124 --> 01:07:16.295
(DOOR SLAMS)

01:07:17.793 --> 01:07:20.362
Jeff, can you hear
what I'm dealing with now?

01:07:20.464 --> 01:07:21.968
It's so uncomfortable
in my own home.

01:07:22.070 --> 01:07:23.465
I don't know if you had
a chance to hear

01:07:23.568 --> 01:07:25.539
what she was saying
when she was screaming.

01:07:25.641 --> 01:07:26.635
JEFF:<i> I heard...</i>

01:07:29.138 --> 01:07:30.309
MARK: Yeah.

01:07:31.141 --> 01:07:32.142
You know what it is?

01:07:32.244 --> 01:07:33.174
Is that you're
fucking jealous

01:07:33.276 --> 01:07:34.715
that I can still go out

01:07:34.818 --> 01:07:36.045
and get drinks
with my friends,

01:07:36.147 --> 01:07:37.411
and it's completely fine.

01:07:37.513 --> 01:07:39.214
And you wish
you could do that.

01:07:39.316 --> 01:07:40.448
Well, stop trying to pretend

01:07:40.550 --> 01:07:42.857
that I'm the one
with the fucking problem.

01:07:42.959 --> 01:07:44.387
MARK: Did you hear that?
JEFF:<i> Yeah.</i>

01:07:44.489 --> 01:07:46.253
-MARK: Yeah, that's her.
-(OBJECTS CLANKING)

01:07:46.355 --> 01:07:47.289
I hope you and Jeff...

01:07:47.391 --> 01:07:49.823
are real fucking
happy together.

01:07:53.098 --> 01:07:54.261
MARK: And she just... I...

01:07:54.363 --> 01:07:55.970
I'm gonna call you back.

01:07:56.073 --> 01:07:57.732
-All right, thanks, Jeff.
-JEFF:<i> Yeah, okay.</i>

01:07:58.607 --> 01:07:59.635
Hey, Dawn?

01:08:00.575 --> 01:08:01.769
Dawn?

01:08:13.552 --> 01:08:15.986
PRIDE DIRECTOR:
Today, we are happy to have

01:08:16.088 --> 01:08:17.586
our greatest fighters

01:08:17.688 --> 01:08:21.963
in one room together
for this press conference.

01:08:22.065 --> 01:08:24.960
Please give a round of
applause for them.

01:08:25.062 --> 01:08:27.267
(ALL APPLAUDING)

01:08:30.470 --> 01:08:34.270
We will be holding
a tournament over two events,

01:08:34.372 --> 01:08:36.471
leading to
a championship fight

01:08:36.573 --> 01:08:39.107
that will result
in the number one fighter

01:08:39.209 --> 01:08:41.747
in all of the world.

01:08:41.849 --> 01:08:43.844
(CROWD APPLAUDING)

01:08:55.529 --> 01:08:59.330
And also, we regret
that we disappointed the fans

01:08:59.433 --> 01:09:03.332
last time with the cancelation
of the main card

01:09:03.434 --> 01:09:07.269
of Enson Inoue
versus Mark Kerr.

01:09:07.371 --> 01:09:09.569
We have received Mark's word

01:09:09.671 --> 01:09:13.077
that this will not
happen again.

01:09:13.180 --> 01:09:15.211
And he has asked
for some time

01:09:15.313 --> 01:09:17.911
to address his Japanese fans

01:09:18.013 --> 01:09:21.849
regarding his inclusion
in this special tournament.

01:09:26.859 --> 01:09:28.289
Hello.

01:09:28.391 --> 01:09:30.359
And thank you to everyone

01:09:30.461 --> 01:09:33.234
for allowing me
to be here today.

01:09:34.269 --> 01:09:37.136
I'd like to apologize,
first and foremost,

01:09:37.238 --> 01:09:41.075
to the Pride organization
and staff.

01:09:41.178 --> 01:09:45.972
You have been
extremely understanding to me

01:09:46.074 --> 01:09:50.515
during my time of dealing
with my personal struggles,

01:09:53.221 --> 01:09:56.624
and finally to
the Japanese people,

01:09:56.726 --> 01:09:57.951
the Japanese fans.

01:09:59.161 --> 01:10:01.724
I know that
you've been questioning

01:10:01.826 --> 01:10:04.925
whether I am the fighter
that you thought that I was.

01:10:07.103 --> 01:10:11.301
And one of
my biggest regrets in life

01:10:11.403 --> 01:10:13.538
is the answer
to that question.

01:10:15.303 --> 01:10:16.475
I wasn't.

01:10:18.178 --> 01:10:19.709
And I'm ashamed about that.

01:10:21.212 --> 01:10:22.983
But I promise you,

01:10:23.085 --> 01:10:24.147
that I'm gonna work
even harder

01:10:24.249 --> 01:10:26.881
to make this up to you.

01:10:28.186 --> 01:10:30.086
Thank you.<i> Arigato.</i>

01:10:30.188 --> 01:10:32.359
(CROWD APPLAUDING)

01:10:34.191 --> 01:10:36.363
(INAUDIBLE)

01:11:13.600 --> 01:11:15.329
-Look what the cat dragged in.
-(MARK CHUCKLING)

01:11:15.431 --> 01:11:18.237
-Marquito!
-Basito.

01:11:18.339 --> 01:11:20.237
-(LAUGHS) What's up, brother?
-Brother.

01:11:20.340 --> 01:11:22.076
-Man, good to see you.
-Mwah.

01:11:22.178 --> 01:11:24.210
Ooh! I guess we got
some work to do.

01:11:24.312 --> 01:11:26.314
-A little bit.
-I'm just kidding, man.

01:11:26.416 --> 01:11:28.712
-Yeah, take a look at this.
-BAS: What do you got?

01:11:29.547 --> 01:11:31.617
MARK: It's the rules.
BAS: Oof!

01:11:32.387 --> 01:11:34.147
Man, they've taken
all your weapons away.

01:11:34.249 --> 01:11:36.518
Yeah. Took everything away.
I mean, Coleman's been working

01:11:36.620 --> 01:11:38.457
on his striking
and his kicking.

01:11:38.559 --> 01:11:40.192
Promoters told him
that they don't want to see

01:11:40.294 --> 01:11:41.755
any more grappling
and wrestling.

01:11:41.857 --> 01:11:43.097
BAS: Yeah, they wanna see
knockouts.

01:11:43.199 --> 01:11:44.624
They want to see people
get knocked out.

01:11:44.727 --> 01:11:46.132
Well, look how
he beat Ricardo.

01:11:46.234 --> 01:11:47.696
Knocked him out, right?
I mean...

01:11:47.798 --> 01:11:49.267
And Enson next year
is gonna do exactly

01:11:49.369 --> 01:11:50.635
-the same thing to you.
-Yeah.

01:11:50.737 --> 01:11:53.073
He's gonna come for you,
and he wants to knock you out.

01:11:53.175 --> 01:11:54.138
You're just gonna
move backwards,

01:11:54.240 --> 01:11:55.173
wait for the right moment,

01:11:55.275 --> 01:11:56.574
shoot in, take his ass down,

01:11:56.676 --> 01:11:58.639
and then you just hit him
in the face, I guess.

01:11:58.741 --> 01:12:01.245
-So, no striking?
-No, no striking.

01:12:01.348 --> 01:12:02.614
Well, you need
to know striking

01:12:02.716 --> 01:12:04.345
in order to get him to tire
to take him to the ground.

01:12:04.447 --> 01:12:05.953
But, come on, man,

01:12:06.055 --> 01:12:07.782
you know his game plan, right?

01:12:07.885 --> 01:12:10.851
Five wins by knockout,
five wins by submission.

01:12:10.953 --> 01:12:13.520
And then, last year,
on my freaking birthday,

01:12:13.622 --> 01:12:15.029
who won the Abu Dhabi

01:12:15.131 --> 01:12:16.894
Combat Club
world championship?

01:12:16.996 --> 01:12:18.493
You did.

01:12:18.595 --> 01:12:19.860
He's not gonna take you down.

01:12:19.962 --> 01:12:22.533
He saw you beat
four amazing grapplers.

01:12:22.635 --> 01:12:24.865
Nobody came even close
to submitting you.

01:12:24.967 --> 01:12:27.774
So trust me,
this guy is not gonna take you

01:12:27.876 --> 01:12:29.009
to the ground.

01:12:29.111 --> 01:12:31.110
-Thank you.
-You ready?

01:12:31.212 --> 01:12:33.675
-I think so.
-You think so?

01:12:33.777 --> 01:12:35.377
Come on, Mark,
it's a yes or no answer.

01:12:35.479 --> 01:12:36.747
(MOCKINGLY) "I think so."

01:12:36.849 --> 01:12:38.380
(IN NORMAL VOICE) That's
right. Come on. Are you ready?

01:12:38.482 --> 01:12:40.251
-Yes.
-Oh! Looky.

01:12:40.353 --> 01:12:41.353
Look at the sight of the show.

01:12:41.455 --> 01:12:43.688
-Marquito... is back.
-(BELL RINGING)

01:12:52.330 --> 01:12:53.698
(ALARM RINGING)

01:12:53.800 --> 01:12:56.269
Uh, actually, we're gonna
have to wait ten seconds...

01:12:56.371 --> 01:12:57.735
(CHUCKLING)
...till the buzzer goes.

01:12:58.435 --> 01:13:00.034
So, deep breaths.

01:13:01.040 --> 01:13:02.440
(EXHALES)

01:13:02.542 --> 01:13:05.413
-(ALARM BEEPING)
-Okay, here we go. Two.

01:13:05.947 --> 01:13:07.580
Good. Again.

01:13:08.380 --> 01:13:10.412
-Four.
-(MARK GRUNTING)

01:13:10.514 --> 01:13:11.914
Good. Uppercut straight.

01:13:12.986 --> 01:13:14.083
Nice.

01:13:14.186 --> 01:13:15.417
Very good.

01:13:15.519 --> 01:13:17.622
Good. Now switch. Boom!

01:13:17.724 --> 01:13:20.428
There we go. You see.
Stop playing with that.

01:13:22.999 --> 01:13:23.992
BAS: How do you feel?

01:13:26.402 --> 01:13:28.832
(CHUCKLES) Good.
That's how you should feel.

01:13:33.239 --> 01:13:35.407
(MARK GRUNTING)

01:13:35.509 --> 01:13:37.577
Okay. Okay.
Mark, Mark, Mark, watch.

01:13:38.744 --> 01:13:40.075
You're looking where
you're gonna hit, right?

01:13:40.177 --> 01:13:43.048
I went to hit you in the head,
well, you're gonna defend it.

01:13:43.150 --> 01:13:44.085
Now, so what I do,

01:13:44.187 --> 01:13:45.448
I hit the body
and I hit it hard

01:13:45.550 --> 01:13:46.613
because he needs to defend it.

01:13:46.715 --> 01:13:47.847
He needs to respect it.

01:13:47.949 --> 01:13:49.782
Boom to the body,
boom to the body.

01:13:49.884 --> 01:13:51.292
Same motto. Boom to the head.

01:13:51.394 --> 01:13:52.990
But you see,
you don't look at the head.

01:13:53.093 --> 01:13:53.887
All right?

01:13:53.989 --> 01:13:55.592
So you hit here, boom!
And you go...

01:13:55.694 --> 01:13:58.026
(BAS GROANS,
BREATHING THROUGH TEETH)

01:13:59.531 --> 01:14:01.033
-MARK: Bas?
-(BAS SOBS)

01:14:01.135 --> 01:14:02.534
MARK: Bas, you okay?

01:14:02.637 --> 01:14:03.830
-He's having a heart attack.
-BAS: No, no, no.

01:14:03.932 --> 01:14:04.998
MARK: Someone call
911 right now.

01:14:05.101 --> 01:14:07.274
BAS: No, no, no.
It's my freakin' tendon, dude.

01:14:07.376 --> 01:14:09.042
-Did you tear it?
-BAS: My ten... No!

01:14:09.144 --> 01:14:10.945
It's messed up my career.

01:14:11.047 --> 01:14:12.544
-(GROANS)
-You okay?

01:14:12.647 --> 01:14:14.380
BAS: No, it's freaking...
It's going to go off

01:14:14.482 --> 01:14:15.675
for an hour and a half.
I know this.

01:14:15.777 --> 01:14:17.111
I've been here many times.

01:14:17.820 --> 01:14:18.816
Shit!

01:14:19.551 --> 01:14:21.082
(MAN SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY)

01:14:23.818 --> 01:14:25.988
(BAS BREATHING SHARPLY)

01:14:34.799 --> 01:14:36.630
BAS: Okay. We need to get
something, guys.

01:14:36.732 --> 01:14:38.339
I think... One is coming.

01:14:38.441 --> 01:14:39.438
I need to go to a hospital
or something.

01:14:39.540 --> 01:14:41.003
MAN: Breathe, breathe.
Breathe, breathe.

01:14:43.112 --> 01:14:45.073
(BAS BREATHING SHAKILY)

01:14:46.515 --> 01:14:47.909
Oh, and it's gonna be
an hour and a half.

01:14:48.012 --> 01:14:49.679
I know this is gonna be
an hour and a half.

01:14:49.781 --> 01:14:51.250
-MAN: Breathe.
-Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

01:14:51.352 --> 01:14:52.751
What's wrong with this one?

01:14:55.022 --> 01:14:56.249
Oh, dude.

01:14:57.260 --> 01:15:00.088
-Ow!
-Okay. Okay. Which one?

01:15:02.131 --> 01:15:03.725
Which one? Which one?

01:15:03.827 --> 01:15:05.098
-BAS: It's this arm.
-This one?

01:15:05.200 --> 01:15:06.534
-Yeah.
-MARK: Okay.

01:15:08.471 --> 01:15:10.568
I'm not using.
I swear to God, I'm clean.

01:15:10.670 --> 01:15:11.898
-This is old.
-I don't give a shit.

01:15:12.000 --> 01:15:13.874
Do anything.
I don't give a shit.

01:15:13.976 --> 01:15:14.971
MARK: Okay.

01:15:17.639 --> 01:15:18.843
(BAS GRUNTS)

01:15:23.348 --> 01:15:25.146
(EXHALING)

01:15:28.019 --> 01:15:30.723
Five seconds, all your pain is
gonna go away.

01:15:31.323 --> 01:15:33.159
Oh, oh, oh.

01:15:33.261 --> 01:15:36.927
Oh, oh, oh. Oh, oh, oh.

01:15:37.527 --> 01:15:40.334
Oh. (EXHALING)

01:15:40.436 --> 01:15:42.130
-Just breathe.
-BAS: Yeah, that's good.

01:15:42.598 --> 01:15:44.336
Oh, dude...

01:15:44.439 --> 01:15:46.205
Oh, dude,
I feel like a plant.

01:15:46.307 --> 01:15:47.971
(CHUCKLES) That's it.

01:15:49.543 --> 01:15:51.073
How do you fight
on that shit?

01:15:53.182 --> 01:15:54.208
You just get used to it.

01:15:54.949 --> 01:15:56.144
Wow.

01:15:57.120 --> 01:15:59.081
Wow, man, that's hot.

01:16:00.355 --> 01:16:01.754
-(EXHALES)
-Just breathe.

01:16:03.151 --> 01:16:05.252
Now I know why
you were always sweaty.

01:16:06.327 --> 01:16:08.254
You were always sweaty.

01:16:08.356 --> 01:16:11.830
-Ooh. This is weird.
-Just breathe. Just breathe.

01:16:14.002 --> 01:16:15.295
BAS: Oh.

01:16:17.104 --> 01:16:18.166
Oh, man.

01:16:19.668 --> 01:16:21.169
Different world.

01:16:22.642 --> 01:16:24.843
<i> (MY WAY</i>
BY FRANK SINATRA PLAYING)

01:16:44.263 --> 01:16:45.292
BAS: Yes!

01:16:48.431 --> 01:16:49.937
Yes!

01:16:50.039 --> 01:16:51.166
Okay. Go around.

01:16:52.074 --> 01:16:53.333
(CHUCKLING)

01:16:55.241 --> 01:16:56.237
BAS: Yes!

01:16:57.308 --> 01:16:58.305
Yes!

01:17:17.100 --> 01:17:18.864
(BOTH GRUNTING)

01:17:41.683 --> 01:17:42.888
Come on.

01:17:45.087 --> 01:17:47.591
-Double cross.
-(BOTH GRUNTING)

01:17:47.693 --> 01:17:49.664
BAS: Good! Take a breather.

01:17:50.792 --> 01:17:51.996
(MARK EXHALES)

01:17:53.663 --> 01:17:55.868
(GRUNTING)

01:18:05.477 --> 01:18:06.846
(GRUNTING)

01:19:08.537 --> 01:19:10.171
STEPHEN QUADROS:<i> Hi,</i>
<i> everybody, and welcome to</i>

01:19:10.274 --> 01:19:12.875
<i> the Pride Grand Prix 2000</i>
<i> opening round.</i>

01:19:12.977 --> 01:19:15.448
<i> Tonight we have</i>
<i> 16 men competing</i>

01:19:15.550 --> 01:19:16.945
<i> in eight different fights.</i>

01:19:17.047 --> 01:19:18.550
One clash
I'm really excited about

01:19:18.653 --> 01:19:20.351
is the clash
between Mark Kerr

01:19:20.453 --> 01:19:21.718
and Enson Inoue.

01:19:21.820 --> 01:19:22.852
Wrestling versus jiu-jitsu.

01:19:22.954 --> 01:19:23.887
That's gonna be
a great one, Bas.

01:19:23.989 --> 01:19:25.252
It's gonna be
a super exciting fight

01:19:25.354 --> 01:19:26.757
and I'll tell you why.
Because last time,

01:19:26.859 --> 01:19:28.562
Mark Kerr wasn't
in the best shape.

01:19:28.664 --> 01:19:30.056
This time, though,
he came back to me.

01:19:30.158 --> 01:19:31.392
And you know as well as I do,

01:19:31.494 --> 01:19:33.531
once you acquire the skill set
of mixed martial arts,

01:19:33.633 --> 01:19:35.066
I think that endurance

01:19:35.168 --> 01:19:37.535
is the most important aspect
of mixed martial arts.

01:19:37.637 --> 01:19:39.139
So he can go the distance.

01:19:39.241 --> 01:19:40.135
Let's hope so.

01:19:40.238 --> 01:19:42.072
Uh, one thing everybody's been
talking about is

01:19:42.174 --> 01:19:44.508
the potential collision
between the two Americans

01:19:44.610 --> 01:19:46.009
in this tournament.

01:19:46.112 --> 01:19:48.914
Bas, have you spoken
to either Kerr or Coleman

01:19:49.016 --> 01:19:51.552
about the thought
of fighting such a good friend

01:19:51.654 --> 01:19:53.014
for a life-changing
amount of money?

01:19:53.116 --> 01:19:54.619
That's
a super intense question,

01:19:54.721 --> 01:19:56.018
Stephen, and, no, I have not.

01:19:56.120 --> 01:19:57.921
<i> But I can only imagine</i>
<i> they're deep</i>

01:19:58.023 --> 01:19:59.420
<i> in each other's heads</i>
<i> right now.</i>

01:20:01.290 --> 01:20:03.556
(POP MUSIC PLAYING
FAINTLY ON SPEAKERS)

01:20:03.859 --> 01:20:05.030
(CHUCKLES)

01:20:06.395 --> 01:20:08.297
-Coleman, you see this?
-COLEMAN: Yeah?

01:20:09.634 --> 01:20:10.937
What page?

01:20:11.900 --> 01:20:13.104
MARK: Seven.

01:20:16.872 --> 01:20:17.971
(CHUCKLES)

01:20:18.073 --> 01:20:19.544
Caught you mid-breath.

01:20:19.646 --> 01:20:22.912
Yeah, I look exhausted.

01:20:23.014 --> 01:20:24.316
MARK: You look
good though, man.

01:20:24.418 --> 01:20:25.550
COLEMAN: Yeah.

01:20:25.652 --> 01:20:27.217
All right, go to five.

01:20:28.554 --> 01:20:29.885
Look at that.

01:20:29.987 --> 01:20:31.322
That's a great one mid-kick.

01:20:31.425 --> 01:20:32.420
(CHUCKLES)

01:20:46.004 --> 01:20:47.435
Coleman, you wanna
have some fun?

01:20:48.773 --> 01:20:50.240
What do you mean?

01:20:51.378 --> 01:20:52.374
Come on.

01:20:53.241 --> 01:20:54.607
COLEMAN: Yeah?
MARK: Yeah.

01:20:56.011 --> 01:20:58.215
(CARS HONKING HORNS)

01:21:10.596 --> 01:21:12.559
(CROWD CHEERING)

01:21:17.238 --> 01:21:18.268
Wow.

01:21:21.875 --> 01:21:23.944
-It's fuckin' cool, man.
-Oh, yeah.

01:21:24.445 --> 01:21:25.407
Lot of people.

01:21:26.613 --> 01:21:27.981
They love you, man.

01:21:28.449 --> 01:21:29.609
They're not...

01:21:30.684 --> 01:21:32.045
Come on, go say hi to 'em.

01:21:32.147 --> 01:21:34.284
Come on, bro, come on.

01:21:36.151 --> 01:21:38.118
(CROWD CONTINUES CHEERING)

01:21:38.220 --> 01:21:40.389
